rimary continuity record.\n\n  Line 48: │  │  │ codex/   │ │save/     │ │ description / continuity │   │  │\n\n  Line 81: │   ├── lib/                # Validation, graph metadata, description, continuity, resume\n\n  Line 106: Spec-kit treats canonical spec documents as the durable continuity record. The generated trigger index is a lookup surface over that record, not the record itself.\n\n  Line 110: 1. Resolve the requested spec folder, following a valid phase-parent `derived.last_active_child_id` into a child before reading continuity.\n\n  Line 112: 3. Fall back to `_memory.continuity` frontmatter blocks inside `implementation-summary.md`.\n\n  Line 118: 2. `generate-context.js` routes content into the right canonical doc (`implementation-summary.md`, `decision-record.md`, `handover.md`) and refreshes `description.json` + `graph-metadata.json`.\n\n  Line 119: 3. There is no second write lane. `generate-context.js` is the only writer of `_memory.continuity`, and it keeps the atomic same-directory update and lock semantics that made a separate indexing call unnecessary.\n\n  Line 124: - `/speckit:resume` owns the read path, walking the continuity ladder above.\n\n  Line 125: - `runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js` owns the write path.\n\n  Line 138: **Discovery and continuity.** `handlers/spec-doc-discovery.ts` walks the filesystem for canonical spec documents and detects a folder's level; `lib/discovery/` re-exports it as a seam so `lib/` code depends inward rather than reaching sideways. `lib/continuity/` owns the bounded continuity record and `lib/resume/` builds the ladder a resume walks.\n\n  Line 144: **Stress tests.** `stress-test/` carries opt-in load and contention suites, excluded from the default test config and run through `vitest.stress.config.ts`.\n\n  Line 159: | `runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js`, `/speckit:save`, `/speckit:search` | The scripts workspace | The continuity writer and the retrieval commands; \"memory\" here is the command family's literal name, not a store |\n\n  Line 180: **Spec folder validation.** `runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh` enforces 20 rules across required files, anchor structure, frontmatter shape, template source markers, continuity freshness, and phase-parent detection. Strict mode treats warnings as failures.\n\n  Line 184: **Test surfaces.** Default `npm test` runs the engine suites through the bounded runner in `runtime/scripts/run-tests.mjs` and, through `runtime/package.json` `test:spec-validation`, the tracked spec-validation shell suites. Stress suites are opt-in via `vitest run --config vitest.stress.config.ts`.\n\n  Line 192: | ADR-001 | Canonical continuity surfaces own the durable record; generated memory is search-only | Accepted |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/README.md:\n  Line 12: > Consolidated TypeScript modules shared between the CLI scripts workspace and the runtime package for embeddings, scoring, normalization, and utility logic. Source files are `.ts`. `shared/` builds as ESM (`package.json` sets `\"type\": \"module\"` and `tsconfig.json` uses NodeNext), with generated output in `shared/dist/`.\n\n  Line 21: - **CLI scripts** (`runtime/cli/`) - `generate-context.ts` and other utilities\n\n  Line 26: These modules support packet-doc-first continuity: `/speckit:resume`, implemented by `.opencode/commands/speckit/resume.md`, rebuilds active context from `handover.md -> _memory.continuity -> spec docs`, while generated continuity support artifacts remain supporting search material.\n\n  Line 169: ├── tsconfig.json               # TypeScript project configuration\n\n  Line 196: │   ├── memory-template-contract.ts    # Template contract validation for continuity support artifacts\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/algorithms/adaptive-fusion.ts:\n  Line 74:   continuity:      { seman