{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788625057453,"sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_FT6UteR3Cz2Z89NgbTYV8drZ","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"system-spec-kit/scripts/|scripts/dist/|scripts/memory|dist/memory|scripts/tests/|scripts/core/|scripts/lib/|scripts/spec/|scripts/runtime/|runtime/runtime|runtime/cli/.*memory|memory/README","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit","include":"*.{md,json,ts,js,cjs,mjs,sh,yml,yaml}"},"output":"Found 100 matches (more matches available)\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/ARCHITECTURE.md:\n  Line 159: | `runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js`, `/speckit:save`, `/speckit:search` | The scripts workspace | The continuity writer and the retrieval commands; \"memory\" here is the command family's literal name, not a store |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/SKILL.md:\n  Line 95: **Typed leaf projection (fleet routing standard).** system-spec-kit is a normal, registry-less single-mode skill whose sole workflow mode is `system-spec-kit` (there is no `mode-registry.json`). Its router routes ONLY into the `references/` and `assets/` doc corpora, so those are the only routable leaves: every one is enumerated in `leaf-manifest.json`, generated from `leaf-manifest.config.json` (`generate-leaf-manifest.cjs --write .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit`; byte-stable under `--check`). `leaf-aliases.json` binds each router-emitted root-relative path (e.g. `references/memory/memory-system.md`) to its typed `(system-spec-kit, leafResourceId)` identity so a deterministic router replay recovers real typed pairs against the manifest. The `RESOURCE_MAP` below emits those exact leaf paths. The rest of the package is deliberately NOT routable: `runtime/cli/`, `runtime/`, `shared/`, `templates/`, `changelog/` and other engine dirs are the spec-kit runtime, and `feature-catalog/` + `manual-testing-playbook/` are runtime-engine capability docs and behavior-test fixtures — no `RESOURCE_MAP` intent selects them, so they are excluded from `leafRoots` and never appear in the manifest. This is an intentionally thin router: it maps spec-folder workflow intents (plan, implement, complete, memory, phase, hooks, …) to a small set of reference docs, while the large playbook chiefly exercises validation and generator behavior rather than doc routing (most scenarios carry empty typed gold). Regenerate `leaf-manifest.json` and keep `leaf-aliases.json` in sync whenever the `references/` or `assets/` corpus changes.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/config/README.md:\n  Line 22: - `config.jsonc` defines the workflow and continuity-writer settings that `scripts/core/config.ts` merges into `SpecKitConfig`: preview and truncation caps, conversation windowing, timezone offset, observation and file limits, and the quality abort threshold.\n\n  Line 23: - `filters.jsonc` defines the noise, dedupe and quality pipeline that `scripts/lib/content-filter.ts` applies to captured session content.\n\n  Line 31: This directory belongs to the `system-spec-kit` skill. Changes should stay compatible with the loaders under `scripts/core/` and `scripts/lib/`.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/assets/template-mapping.md:\n  Line 272: **Generation:** Use `/speckit:save` or `node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js --json '{\"specFolder\":\"###-name\",\"sessionSummary\":\"...\"}' specs/###-name/` to update the packet's canonical continuity surfaces, primarily `_memory.continuity` inside `implementation-summary.md`.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v3.9.0.0.md:\n  Line 47: | `scripts/lib/validator-registry.json` | Registered `SCOPE_ADHERENCE` |\n\n  Line 51: | `scripts/tests/research-template-gating.vitest.ts` | New: research-template gating coverage |\n\n  Line 52: | `scripts/tests/check-scope-adherence.vitest.ts` | New: scope-rule coverage |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v3.5.0.0.md:\n  Line 139: **Verify and repair with `/doctor`.** After upgrading, the doctor command is the fastest way to confirm each subsystem is healthy. `/doctor <target>` runs a focused diagnostic for `memory`, `embeddings`, `causal-graph`, `code-graph`, `deep-loop`, `skill-advisor` or `skill-budget`. Most targets are read-only and report drift with a recommended action rather than mutating anything. `/doctor:mcp install|debug` covers the MCP launcher and daemon infrastructure, and `/doctor:update` runs a dependency-ordered cross-subsystem alignment with snapshot, validate and rollback. For a quick read-only install check, `bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/doctor.sh --strict` confirms the memory server's dist and native modules are present.\n\n  Line 141: **Recycle the daemon after a dist change.** Because many sessions now share one memory daemon, a pulled change to the compiled server only takes effect once that daemon recycles. `dist/` is gitignored, so rebuild after every pull. `bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/deploy-mcp.sh` rebuilds every MCP dist, and `--recycle` performs the transparent daemon-child recycle that keeps clients connected. A rebuilt `shared/dist`, where the embedding resolver lives, also needs a recycle to take effect.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/tsconfig.json:\n  Line 51:     \"scripts/tests/**\",\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v3.0.0.3.md:\n  Line 43: | `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/migrate-deep-research-paths.ts` | Added | Migration utility for the path change |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/retrieval/session-recovery-spec-kit-resume.md:\n  Line 76: | `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/continuity/generate-context.ts` | Script | Continuity writer: produces the `_memory.continuity` block the ladder reads |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/feature-flag-reference/runtime-config-contract.md:\n  Line 87: | `runtime/cli/tests/runtime-memory-inputs.vitest.ts` | Automated test | Legacy `qualityAbortThreshold` normalization and explicit config-input failure handling in the script runtime |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v3.1.2.0.md:\n  Line 148: When `scripts/dist/memory/validate-memory-quality.js` was not built, the V-rule bridge returned a successful \"unavailable\" result. Saves would succeed without any quality validation. The bridge now fails closed -- it returns a failure result that blocks the save and surfaces a clear \"build scripts first\" error. A `SPECKIT_VRULE_OPTIONAL` environment variable allows development workflows to opt out.\n\n  Line 219: | `scripts/core/workflow.ts` | Lazy mcp-server adapter |\n\n  Line 220: | `scripts/lib/validate-memory-quality.ts` | V8 descendant detection, `related_specs` allowlist |\n\n  Line 228: | `scripts/tests/` (5 files) | Mock fixes, V8 regression test |\n\n  Line 246: | `scripts/core/workflow.ts` | the try import mcp api helper helper |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v3.4.2.0.md:\n  Line 113: - **Comment hygiene is now detectable.** `node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/validation/ephemeral-pointer-audit.mjs <paths>` reports ephemeral-artifact pointers in code comments and exits nonzero on any hit. Wiring it into pre-commit or CI is a follow-on opt-in.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:\n  Line 354: `runtime/cli/extractors/` feeds the continuity writer, not a memory index.\n\n  Line 596: `runtime/cli/spec-folder/generate-description.ts` is the surviving producer; the vector-search short-circuit it used to feed went with the memory engine.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v3.0.0.4.md:\n  Line 55: 4. Verify: `SPECKIT_ABLATION=true npx tsx .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/evals/run-ablation.ts` should complete without alignment errors\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v1+/v1.2.3.0.md:\n  Line 32: | `scripts/memory/generate-context.js` | Referenced in the original changelog. |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v2+/v2.3.0.2.md:\n  Line 57: | `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/lib/structure-aware-chunker.ts` | New structure-aware chunker (not yet wired). |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/memory-quality-and-indexing/spec-folder-description-discovery.md:\n  Line 101: | `runtime/cli/core/workflow.ts` | Core | Memory tracking integration (`memorySequence` increment, `memoryNameHistory` ring buffer, and invalid-value hardening via `Number()` coercion) |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v3.2.0.1.md:\n  Line 55: | `scripts/core/workflow.ts` | Session ID passthrough; size-based dup