{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788625084317,"sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_QaYUInYrqZllc2J2HPe2aIJR","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md","offset":1,"limit":180},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Spec Scripts\"\n3: description: \"Spec lifecycle shell entrypoints for create, upgrade, validation, completion checks and archival.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"spec scripts\"\n6:   - \"upgrade spec level\"\n7:   - \"validate spec folder\"\n8:   - \"check placeholders\"\n9: ---\n10: \n11: # Spec Scripts\n12: \n13: ---\n14: \n15: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n16: \n17: `scripts/spec/` owns shell entrypoints for spec folder lifecycle work. It creates packet folders, upgrades documentation levels, validates structure, checks completion state and archives finished or stale folders.\n18: \n19: Current state:\n20: \n21: - Shell scripts are the public command surface for spec lifecycle operations.\n22: - Validation delegates rule checks to `../rules/` and shared helpers in `../lib/`.\n23: - Scripts accept explicit spec folder paths and are intended to run from the repository root.\n24: \n25: ---\n26: \n27: ## 2. ARCHITECTURE\n28: \n29: ```text\n30: ╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n31: │                         SPEC SCRIPTS                         │\n32: ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n33: \n34: ┌──────────────┐      ┌────────────────┐      ┌────────────────┐\n35: │ Operator     │ ───▶ │ create.sh      │ ───▶ │ Spec folder    │\n36: │ or command   │      │ upgrade-level  │      │ files          │\n37: └──────┬───────┘      └───────┬────────┘      └───────┬────────┘\n38:        │                      │                       │\n39:        │                      ▼                       ▼\n40:        │              ┌──────────────┐       ┌────────────────┐\n41:        └────────────▶ │ validate.sh  │ ───▶  │ rules/check-*  │\n42:                       └──────┬───────┘       └───────┬────────┘\n43:                              │                       │\n44:                              ▼                       ▼\n45:                       ┌──────────────┐       ┌────────────────┐\n46:                       │ completion   │       │ lib/*.sh       │\n47:                       │ and archive  │       │ helpers        │\n48:                       └──────────────┘       └────────────────┘\n49: \n50: Dependency direction: spec/*.sh ───▶ rules/*.sh ───▶ lib/*.sh\n51: ```\n52: \n53: ---\n54: \n55: ## 3. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n56: \n57: ```text\n58: scripts/spec/\n59: +-- create.sh                    # Scaffold spec folders from templates\n60: +-- upgrade-level.sh             # Add level-owned docs and sections\n61: +-- check-placeholders.sh        # Detect unresolved template placeholders\n62: +-- validate.sh                  # Run structural validation rules\n63: +-- progressive-validate.sh      # Staged validation helper\n64: +-- check-completion.sh          # Verify completion checklist state\n65: +-- scaffold-debug-delegation.sh # Generate debug-delegation handoff scaffolds\n66: +-- calculate-completeness.sh    # Report checklist completion metrics\n67: +-- recommend-level.sh           # Recommend documentation level from task signals\n68: +-- archive.sh                   # Move completed or stale spec folders\n69: +-- check-template-staleness.sh  # Compare generated docs with templates\n70: +-- check-smart-router.sh        # Validate SKILL.md smart-router references\n71: +-- quality-audit.sh             # Batch quality audit helper\n72: +-- test-validation.sh           # Legacy wrapper for scripts/tests/test-validation.sh\n73: +-- is-phase-parent.ts           # Phase-parent detection and manifest health check\n74: +-- sync-phase-map-status.ts     # Sync a phase parent's map table and completion percentages\n75: +-- repair-derived.cjs           # Repair packet facts derivable from disk; refuses authored facts\n76: +-- README-repair-derived.md     # Derived-vs-authored repair boundary reference\n77: `-- README.md\n78: ```\n79: \n80: Allowed direction:\n81: \n82: - `spec/*.sh` may source shared shell helpers from `../lib/`.\n83: - `validate.sh` may call validation rules from `../rules/`.\n84: - Lifecycle scripts may read templates and write only the selected spec folder.\n85: \n86: Disallowed direction:\n87: \n88: - Rule scripts should not mutate spec content.\n89: - Shell helpers should not call spec lifecycle entrypoints.\n90: - Source modules should not import generated `dist/` output directly. Shell entrypoints may execute freshness-verified compiled output, as `validate.sh` does for the runtime validation orchestrator.\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: ## 4. KEY FILES\n95: \n96: | File | Role |\n97: |---|---|\n98: | `create.sh` | Creates new Level 1 or phase folders from templates. |\n99: | `upgrade-level.sh` | Adds missing files and sections for higher documentation levels. |\n100: | `validate.sh` | Runs the modular validation gate used before completion claims. `resolve_orchestrator()` checks the compiled runtime dist freshness (via `../lib/dist-freshness.cjs`) before trusting it and fails closed with exit `3` when stale — no silent auto-rebuild. |\n101: | `check-completion.sh` | Confirms checklist evidence before a task is called complete. |\n102: | `scaffold-debug-delegation.sh` | Generates `debug-delegation.md` handoff scaffolds from failure-trail input. |\n103: | `progressive-validate.sh` | Runs a staged validation pass for detect, fix, suggest and report flows. |\n104: | `check-smart-router.sh` | Validates `SKILL.md` smart-router resource paths and reports load bloat warnings. |\n105: | `test-validation.sh` | Legacy wrapper forwarding to `scripts/tests/test-validation.sh`. |\n106: | `archive.sh` | Moves completed or stale spec folders into the archive area. |\n107: | `is-phase-parent.ts` | Detects whether a folder is a phase parent and reports child-count manifest health. |\n108: | `sync-phase-map-status.ts` | Corrects a phase parent's map table rows and descendant completion percentages. |\n109: | `repair-derived.cjs` | Repairs derivable packet facts (folder name, packet pointer, level, metadata fingerprint) and refuses authored ones; see `README-repair-derived.md`. |\n110: \n111: ---\n112: \n113: ## 5. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n114: \n115: Main validation flow:\n116: \n117: ```text\n118: ╭──────────────────────────────╮\n119: │ Repository-root command      │\n120: ╰──────────────────────────────╯\n121:               │\n122:               ▼\n123: ┌──────────────────────────────┐\n124: │ validate.sh                  │\n125: └──────────────┬───────────────┘\n126:                ▼\n127: ┌──────────────────────────────┐\n128: │ Load lib shell helpers       │\n129: └──────────────┬───────────────┘\n130:                ▼\n131: ┌──────────────────────────────┐\n132: │ Run rules/check-*.sh         │\n133: └──────────────┬───────────────┘\n134:                ▼\n135: ┌──────────────────────────────┐\n136: │ Print pass, warning or error │\n137: └──────────────────────────────┘\n138: ```\n139: \n140: This folder owns shell orchestration only. Template content belongs under `templates/`, validation rule behavior belongs under `rules/` and shared shell primitives belong under `lib/`.\n141: \n142: ---\n143: \n144: ## 6. ENTRYPOINTS\n145: \n146: ```bash\n147: bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh specs/<name>\n148: bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/upgrade-level.sh specs/<name> --to 3\n149: bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/check-placeholders.sh specs/<name>\n150: bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/<name> --strict\n151: bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/check-completion.sh specs/<name>\n152: ```\n153: \n154: ---\n155: \n156: ## 7. VALIDATION\n157: \n158: Use repository-root commands:\n159: \n160: ```bash\n161: bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/<name> --strict\n162: bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/check-completion.sh specs/<name>\n163: ```\n164: \n165: Use `--recursive` with `validate.sh` when the target is a phase parent with child phase folders.\n166: \n167: ---\n168: \n169: ## 8. RELATED\n170: \n171: - [`README-repair-derived.md`](./README-repair-derived.md)\n172: - [`../README.md`](../README.md)\n173: - [`../lib/README.md`](../lib/README.md)\n174: - [`../rules/README.md`](../rules/README.md)\n175: - [`../templates/README.md`](../templates/README.md)\n\n(End of file - total 175 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Spec Scripts\"\ndescription: \"Spec lifecycle shell entrypoints for create, upgrade, validation, completion checks and archival.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"spec scripts\"\n  - \"upgrade spec level\"\n  - \"validate spec folder\"\n  - \"check placeholders\"\n---\n\n# Spec Scripts\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/spec/` owns shell entrypoints for spec folder lifecycle work. It creates packet folders, upgrades documentation levels, validates structure, checks completion state and archives finished or stale folders.\n\nCurrent state:\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Spec Scripts\"\ndescription: \"Spec lifecycle shell entrypoints for create, upgrade, validation, completion checks and archival.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"spec scripts\"\n  - \"upgrade spec level\"\n  - \"validate spec folder\"\n  - \"check placeholders\"\n---\n\n# Spec Scripts\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/spec/` owns shell entrypoints for spec folder lifecycle work. It creates packet folders, upgrades documentation levels, validates structure, checks completion state and archives finished or stale folders.\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- Shell scripts are the public command surface for spec lifecycle operations.\n- Validation delegates rule checks to `../rules/` and shared helpers in `../lib/`.\n- Scripts accept explicit spec folder paths and are intended to run from the repository root.\n\n---\n\n## 2. ARCHITECTURE\n\n```text\n╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│                         SPEC SCRIPTS                         │\n╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n┌──────────────┐      ┌────────────────┐      ┌────────────────┐\n│ Operator     │ ───▶ │ create.sh      │ ───▶ │ Spec folder    │\n│ or command   │      │ upgrade-level  │      │ files          │\n└──────┬───────┘      └───────┬────────┘      └───────┬────────┘\n       │                      │                       │\n       │                      ▼                       ▼\n       │              ┌──────────────┐       ┌────────────────┐\n       └────────────▶ │ validate.sh  │ ───▶  │ rules/check-*  │\n                      └──────┬───────┘       └───────┬────────┘\n                             │                       │\n                             ▼                       ▼\n                      ┌──────────────┐       ┌────────────────┐\n                      │ completion   │       │ lib/*.sh       │\n                      │ and archive  │       │ helpers        │\n                      └──────────────┘       └────────────────┘\n\nDependency direction: spec/*.sh ───▶ rules/*.sh ───▶ lib/*.sh\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n\n```text\nscripts/spec/\n+-- create.sh                    # Scaffold spec folders from templates\n+-- upgrade-level.sh             # Add level-owned docs and sections\n+-- check-placeholders.sh        # Detect unresolved template placeholders\n+-- validate.sh                  # Run structural validation rules\n+-- progressive-validate.sh      # Staged validation helper\n+-- check-completion.sh          # Verify completion checklist state\n+-- scaffold-debug-delegation.sh # Generate debug-delegation handoff scaffolds\n+-- calculate-completeness.sh    # Report checklist completion metrics\n+-- recommend-level.sh           # Recommend documentation level from task signals\n+-- archive.sh                   # Move completed or stale spec folders\n+-- check-template-staleness.sh  # Compare generated docs with templates\n+-- check-smart-router.sh        # Validate SKILL.md smart-router references\n+-- quality-audit.sh             # Batch quality audit helper\n+-- test-validation.sh           # Legacy wrapper for scripts/tests/test-validation.sh\n+-- is-phase-parent.ts           # Phase-parent detection and manifest health check\n+-- sync-phase-map-status.ts     # Sync a phase parent's map table and completion percentages\n+-- repair-derived.cjs           # Repair packet facts derivable from disk; refuses authored facts\n+-- README-repair-derived.md     # Derived-vs-authored repair boundary reference\n`-- README.md\n```\n\nAllowed direction:\n\n- `spec/*.sh` may source shared shell helpers from `../lib/`.\n- `validate.sh` may call validation rules from `../rules/`.\n- Lifecycle scripts may read templates and write only the selected spec folder.\n\nDisallowed direction:\n\n- Rule scripts should not mutate spec content.\n- Shell helpers should not call spec lifecycle entrypoints.\n- Source modules should not import generated `dist/` output directly. Shell entrypoints may execute freshness-verified compiled output, as `validate.sh` does for the runtime validation orchestrator.\n\n---\n\n## 4. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `create.sh` | Creates new Level 1 or phase folders from templates. |\n| `upgrade-level.sh` | Adds missing files and sections for higher documentation levels. |\n| `validate.sh` | Runs the modular validation gate used before completion claims. `resolve_orchestrator()` checks the compiled runtime dist freshness (via `../lib/dist-freshness.cjs`) before trusting it and fails closed with exit `3` when stale — no silent auto-rebuild. |\n| `check-completion.sh` | Confirms checklist evidence before a task is called complete. |\n| `scaffold-debug-delegation.sh` | Generates `debug-delegation.md` handoff scaffolds from failure-trail input. |\n| `progressive-validate.sh` | Runs a staged validation pass for detect, fix, suggest and report flows. |\n| `check-smart-router.sh` | Validates `SKILL.md` smart-router resource paths and reports load bloat warnings. |\n| `test-validation.sh` | Legacy wrapper forwarding to `scripts/tests/test-validation.sh`. |\n| `archive.sh` | Moves completed or stale spec folders into the archive area. |\n| `is-phase-parent.ts` | Detects whether a folder is a phase parent and reports child-count manifest health. |\n| `sync-phase-map-status.ts` | Corrects a phase parent's map table rows and descendant completion percentages. |\n| `repair-derived.cjs` | Repairs derivable packet facts (folder name, packet pointer, level, metadata fingerprint) and refuses authored ones; see `README-repair-derived.md`. |\n\n---\n\n## 5. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n\nMain validation flow:\n\n```text\n╭──────────────────────────────╮\n│ Repository-root command      │\n╰──────────────────────────────╯\n              │\n              ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────┐\n│ validate.sh                  │\n└──────────────┬───────────────┘\n               ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────┐\n│ Load lib shell helpers       │\n└──────────────┬───────────────┘\n               ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────┐\n│ Run rules/check-*.sh         │\n└──────────────┬───────────────┘\n               ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────┐\n│ Print pass, warning or error │\n└──────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\nThis folder owns shell orchestration only. Template content belongs under `templates/`, validation rule behavior belongs under `rules/` and shared shell primitives belong under `lib/`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. ENTRYPOINTS\n\n```bash\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh specs/<name>\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/upgrade-level.sh specs/<name> --to 3\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/check-placeholders.sh specs/<name>\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/<name> --strict\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/check-completion.sh specs/<name>\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. VALIDATION\n\nUse repository-root commands:\n\n```bash\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/<name> --strict\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/check-completion.sh specs/<name>\n```\n\nUse `--recursive` with `validate.sh` when the target is a phase parent with child phase folders.\n\n---\n\n## 8. RELATED\n\n- [`README-repair-derived.md`](./README-repair-derived.md)\n- [`../README.md`](../README.md)\n- [`../lib/README.md`](../lib/README.md)\n- [`../rules/README.md`](../rules/README.md)\n- [`../templates/README.md`](../templates/README.md)","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":175,"totalLines":175,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md","time":{"start":1788625084312,"end":1788625084315}},"id":"prt_0725cde2a001EHdalY3i133zd3","sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","messageID":"msg_0725cccef001d7VQtW61cOk05C"}}
