{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788625214906,"sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_12ty67KLhKs2j0vgyfGeSTUy","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md","offset":1,"limit":100},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Spec-Folder Detection and Description Metadata\"\n3: description: \"Spec-folder detection, alignment validation, memory-directory setup, and description-metadata generation for the session-capturing and save workflow.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"spec-folder detection and description metadata\"\n6:   - \"folder-detector\"\n7:   - \"detect spec folder\"\n8:   - \"alignment validator\"\n9:   - \"generate-description\"\n10: version: 3.6.0.7\n11: ---\n12: \n13: # Spec-Folder Detection and Description Metadata\n14: \n15: <!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n16: \n17: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n18: \n19: Spec-Folder Detection and Description Metadata is the script surface that decides which spec folder a session belongs to, validates that choice against conversation content, prepares the target spec-doc record directory, and maintains the per-folder description metadata used elsewhere in the system.\n20: \n21: This audited slice combines interactive and deterministic folder selection, content-alignment safety checks, path-safety enforcement, and the CLI used to generate or refresh per-folder `description.json` metadata.\n22: \n23: ---\n24: \n25: ## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n26: \n27: The shipped behavior in this slice currently works as follows:\n28: \n29: 1. `folder-detector.ts` resolves spec folders through a ranked priority chain rather than a single heuristic. It first honors an explicit CLI argument, then a structured-data `SPEC_FOLDER` value, then git-status evidence, current-working-directory inference, session-activity signals, and finally a full auto-detect ranking across available spec folders. The session-learning DB lookup that once sat in this chain (a SQLite `session_learning` table read) was retired along with the memory database; the ranking and candidate-scoring helpers it shared with auto-detect remain and are covered by the test suite's regression cases.\n30: 2. Explicit paths are constrained to approved roots under `specs/` or `.opencode/specs/`, support nested parent/child references, and can recover from multi-segment or basename-only inputs via child-folder search. When an explicit folder is found, alignment is still checked so the workflow can warn about mismatches without overriding the caller's direct selection.\n31: 3. Candidate quality scoring downgrades archive, test-fixture, and scratch-like folders before ranking. Auto-detect ranking then layers multiple signals in order: folder quality, git-status count, session-activity boost, effective depth, recently active child count, numeric ID-vector ordering, modification time, and canonical path tiebreakers.\n32: 4. Git-status ranking counts changed files that fall under candidate spec paths, while session-activity ranking uses a structured signal builder that combines matching tool-call paths, git-changed files, and transcript mentions. Both signals are treated as confidence-checked hints rather than unconditional selectors.\n33: 5. `alignment-validator.ts` extracts conversation topics from recent requests and early observations, expands that with observation keywords from titles, narratives, and filenames, and then computes word-boundary alignment scores against spec-folder path segments instead of using weaker substring matching.\n34: 6. The same validator detects whether the session is primarily `.opencode/` infrastructure work. When enough touched files fall under OpenCode infrastructure paths, it applies a domain-aware bonus only for matching infrastructure-oriented folder names and emits explicit mismatch warnings when the selected folder does not fit the detected subpath.\n35: 7. Before content or folder alignment proceeds, telemetry schema/docs drift validation compares interface fields in `retrieval-telemetry.ts` and the telemetry `README.md`. Field-level drift becomes a hard error, which makes this module a gatekeeper for alignment safety and telemetry documentation consistency at the same time.\n36: 8. `validateContentAlignment()` is the stricter guard. It can recommend higher-scoring alternative folders, warn on moderate matches, and hard-block non-interactive execution when alignment is critically low or when a 0% infrastructure mismatch would otherwise silently route work into the wrong folder.\n37: 9. `validateFolderAlignment()` is the lighter check used when a structured `SPEC_FOLDER` is already present. It still scores alignment, offers better alternatives in interactive mode, and warns on mismatches, but it is more permissive than the content-level gate.\n38: 10. `directory-setup.ts` sanitizes the chosen path against configured specs directories, enforces an `NNN-name` leaf-folder format, refuses missing or non-directory targets, and then creates the `memory/` subdirectory with structured error reporting for permission and disk-space failures.\n39: 11. `generate-description.ts` is the CLI for per-folder `description.json` creation. It resolves real paths to prevent traversal and prefix-bypass attacks, accepts either an explicit `--description` string or a `spec.md`-derived description path, preserves `memorySequence` and `memoryNameHistory` from existing metadata, and writes the refreshed description through the MCP-server API helpers.\n40: 12. `spec-folder/index.ts` is the public barrel for this subsystem. It exports detection, archive filtering, alignment configuration, topic extraction, scoring, telemetry-drift validation, folder-alignment validation, and memory-directory setup as one reusable surface for the rest of the scripts layer.\n41: \n42: ---\n43: \n44: ## 3. SOURCE FILES\n45: \n46: ### Implementation\n47: \n48: | File | Layer | Role |\n49: |------|-------|------|\n50: | `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/folder-detector.ts` | Detection/orchestration | Multi-priority spec-folder resolution, candidate ranking, low-confidence handling, and explicit-path recovery |\n51: | `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/alignment-validator.ts` | Validation | Topic extraction, domain-aware alignment scoring, telemetry schema/docs drift checks, and interactive/non-interactive alignment gating |\n52: | `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/directory-setup.ts` | Filesystem setup | Path sanitization, `NNN-name` enforcement, existence validation, and `memory/` directory creation |\n53: | `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/generate-description.ts` | CLI | Generates or refreshes per-folder `description.json` metadata from explicit text or `spec.md` content |\n54: | `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/index.ts` | Barrel export | Re-exports the spec-folder detection, validation, and setup API surface |\n55: \n56: ---\n57: \n58: ## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n59: - Group: Tooling And Scripts\n60: - Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n61: - Feature file path: `tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md`\n62: Related references:\n63: - [session-extraction-and-enrichment.md](../../feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/session-extraction-and-enrichment.md) — Session Extraction and Enrichment\n64: - [setup-native-module-health-and-mcp-installation.md](../../feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/setup-native-module-health-and-mcp-installation.md) — Setup, Native Module Health, and MCP Installation\n\n(End of file - total 64 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Spec-Folder Detection and Description Metadata\"\ndescription: \"Spec-folder detection, alignment validation, memory-directory setup, and description-metadata generation for the session-capturing and save workflow.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"spec-folder detection and description metadata\"\n  - \"folder-detector\"\n  - \"detect spec folder\"\n  - \"alignment validator\"\n  - \"generate-description\"\nversion: 3.6.0.7\n---\n\n# Spec-Folder Detection and Description Metadata\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nSpec-Folder Detection and Description Metadata is the script surface that decides which spec folder a session belongs to, validates that choice against conversation content, prepares the target spec-doc record directory, and maintains the per-folder description metadata used elsewhere in the system.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Spec-Folder Detection and Description Metadata\"\ndescription: \"Spec-folder detection, alignment validation, memory-directory setup, and description-metadata generation for the session-capturing and save workflow.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"spec-folder detection and description metadata\"\n  - \"folder-detector\"\n  - \"detect spec folder\"\n  - \"alignment validator\"\n  - \"generate-description\"\nversion: 3.6.0.7\n---\n\n# Spec-Folder Detection and Description Metadata\n\n<!-- sk-doc-template: skill_asset_feature_catalog -->\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nSpec-Folder Detection and Description Metadata is the script surface that decides which spec folder a session belongs to, validates that choice against conversation content, prepares the target spec-doc record directory, and maintains the per-folder description metadata used elsewhere in the system.\n\nThis audited slice combines interactive and deterministic folder selection, content-alignment safety checks, path-safety enforcement, and the CLI used to generate or refresh per-folder `description.json` metadata.\n\n---\n\n## 2. HOW IT WORKS\n\nThe shipped behavior in this slice currently works as follows:\n\n1. `folder-detector.ts` resolves spec folders through a ranked priority chain rather than a single heuristic. It first honors an explicit CLI argument, then a structured-data `SPEC_FOLDER` value, then git-status evidence, current-working-directory inference, session-activity signals, and finally a full auto-detect ranking across available spec folders. The session-learning DB lookup that once sat in this chain (a SQLite `session_learning` table read) was retired along with the memory database; the ranking and candidate-scoring helpers it shared with auto-detect remain and are covered by the test suite's regression cases.\n2. Explicit paths are constrained to approved roots under `specs/` or `.opencode/specs/`, support nested parent/child references, and can recover from multi-segment or basename-only inputs via child-folder search. When an explicit folder is found, alignment is still checked so the workflow can warn about mismatches without overriding the caller's direct selection.\n3. Candidate quality scoring downgrades archive, test-fixture, and scratch-like folders before ranking. Auto-detect ranking then layers multiple signals in order: folder quality, git-status count, session-activity boost, effective depth, recently active child count, numeric ID-vector ordering, modification time, and canonical path tiebreakers.\n4. Git-status ranking counts changed files that fall under candidate spec paths, while session-activity ranking uses a structured signal builder that combines matching tool-call paths, git-changed files, and transcript mentions. Both signals are treated as confidence-checked hints rather than unconditional selectors.\n5. `alignment-validator.ts` extracts conversation topics from recent requests and early observations, expands that with observation keywords from titles, narratives, and filenames, and then computes word-boundary alignment scores against spec-folder path segments instead of using weaker substring matching.\n6. The same validator detects whether the session is primarily `.opencode/` infrastructure work. When enough touched files fall under OpenCode infrastructure paths, it applies a domain-aware bonus only for matching infrastructure-oriented folder names and emits explicit mismatch warnings when the selected folder does not fit the detected subpath.\n7. Before content or folder alignment proceeds, telemetry schema/docs drift validation compares interface fields in `retrieval-telemetry.ts` and the telemetry `README.md`. Field-level drift becomes a hard error, which makes this module a gatekeeper for alignment safety and telemetry documentation consistency at the same time.\n8. `validateContentAlignment()` is the stricter guard. It can recommend higher-scoring alternative folders, warn on moderate matches, and hard-block non-interactive execution when alignment is critically low or when a 0% infrastructure mismatch would otherwise silently route work into the wrong folder.\n9. `validateFolderAlignment()` is the lighter check used when a structured `SPEC_FOLDER` is already present. It still scores alignment, offers better alternatives in interactive mode, and warns on mismatches, but it is more permissive than the content-level gate.\n10. `directory-setup.ts` sanitizes the chosen path against configured specs directories, enforces an `NNN-name` leaf-folder format, refuses missing or non-directory targets, and then creates the `memory/` subdirectory with structured error reporting for permission and disk-space failures.\n11. `generate-description.ts` is the CLI for per-folder `description.json` creation. It resolves real paths to prevent traversal and prefix-bypass attacks, accepts either an explicit `--description` string or a `spec.md`-derived description path, preserves `memorySequence` and `memoryNameHistory` from existing metadata, and writes the refreshed description through the MCP-server API helpers.\n12. `spec-folder/index.ts` is the public barrel for this subsystem. It exports detection, archive filtering, alignment configuration, topic extraction, scoring, telemetry-drift validation, folder-alignment validation, and memory-directory setup as one reusable surface for the rest of the scripts layer.\n\n---\n\n## 3. SOURCE FILES\n\n### Implementation\n\n| File | Layer | Role |\n|------|-------|------|\n| `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/folder-detector.ts` | Detection/orchestration | Multi-priority spec-folder resolution, candidate ranking, low-confidence handling, and explicit-path recovery |\n| `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/alignment-validator.ts` | Validation | Topic extraction, domain-aware alignment scoring, telemetry schema/docs drift checks, and interactive/non-interactive alignment gating |\n| `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/directory-setup.ts` | Filesystem setup | Path sanitization, `NNN-name` enforcement, existence validation, and `memory/` directory creation |\n| `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/generate-description.ts` | CLI | Generates or refreshes per-folder `description.json` metadata from explicit text or `spec.md` content |\n| `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/index.ts` | Barrel export | Re-exports the spec-folder detection, validation, and setup API surface |\n\n---\n\n## 4. SOURCE METADATA\n- Group: Tooling And Scripts\n- Canonical catalog source: `feature-catalog.md`\n- Feature file path: `tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md`\nRelated references:\n- [session-extraction-and-enrichment.md](../../feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/session-extraction-and-enrichment.md) — Session Extraction and Enrichment\n- [setup-native-module-health-and-mcp-installation.md](../../feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/setup-native-module-health-and-mcp-installation.md) — Setup, Native Module Health, and MCP Installation","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":64,"totalLines":64,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/tooling-and-scripts/spec-folder-detection-and-description.md","time":{"start":1788625214880,"end":1788625214896}},"id":"prt_0725edd9f001oKU6063zM7mfDc","sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","messageID":"msg_0725e6df90015NzU5Sme7JsUYf"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788625214907,"sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_Z6ga8b0BsOFJFDBnhb3tcS9O","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/config/README.md","offset":1,"limit":120},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/config/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Config Scripts: Barrel Exports\"\n3: description: \"Stable script-side import boundary for system-spec-kit config utilities.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"scripts config barrel\"\n6:   - \"system spec kit config imports\"\n7:   - \"spec directory config\"\n8: ---\n9: \n10: # Config Scripts: Barrel Exports\n11: \n12: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n13: \n14: `scripts/config/` exposes config and specs-directory utilities to script modules without requiring those modules to import from `scripts/core` directly.\n15: \n16: Current state:\n17: \n18: - Re-exports the canonical `CONFIG` object.\n19: - Re-exports specs directory discovery helpers.\n20: - Preserves the dependency boundary between non-core scripts and core config implementation.\n21: \n22: ---\n23: \n24: ## 2. DIRECTORY TREE\n25: \n26: ```text\n27: config/\n28: `-- index.ts\n29: ```\n30: \n31: ---\n32: \n33: ## 3. KEY FILES\n34: \n35: | File | Role |\n36: |---|---|\n37: | `index.ts` | Barrel export for `CONFIG`, specs directory helpers, and config types from `../core/config.js`. |\n38: \n39: ---\n40: \n41: ## 4. BOUNDARIES\n42: \n43: Non-core scripts should import config through this folder. The canonical config implementation remains in `scripts/core/config.ts`.\n44: \n45: Allowed direction:\n46: \n47: ```text\n48: extractors/renderers/loaders -> scripts/config -> scripts/core/config\n49: ```\n50: \n51: ---\n52: \n53: ## 5. VALIDATION\n54: \n55: Run the relevant TypeScript or package test command from the repository root after changing exports.\n56: \n57: ---\n58: \n59: ## 6. RELATED\n60: \n61: - `../core/config.ts`\n62: - `../graph/README.md`\n63: - `../observability/README.md`\n\n(End of file - total 63 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Config Scripts: Barrel Exports\"\ndescription: \"Stable script-side import boundary for system-spec-kit config utilities.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"scripts config barrel\"\n  - \"system spec kit config imports\"\n  - \"spec directory config\"\n---\n\n# Config Scripts: Barrel Exports\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/config/` exposes config and specs-directory utilities to script modules without requiring those modules to import from `scripts/core` directly.\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- Re-exports the canonical `CONFIG` object.\n- Re-exports specs directory discovery helpers.\n- Preserves the dependency boundary between non-core scripts and core config implementation.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/config/README.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Config Scripts: Barrel Exports\"\ndescription: \"Stable script-side import boundary for system-spec-kit config utilities.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"scripts config barrel\"\n  - \"system spec kit config imports\"\n  - \"spec directory config\"\n---\n\n# Config Scripts: Barrel Exports\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/config/` exposes config and specs-directory utilities to script modules without requiring those modules to import from `scripts/core` directly.\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- Re-exports the canonical `CONFIG` object.\n- Re-exports specs directory discovery helpers.\n- Preserves the dependency boundary between non-core scripts and core config implementation.\n\n---\n\n## 2. DIRECTORY TREE\n\n```text\nconfig/\n`-- index.ts\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `index.ts` | Barrel export for `CONFIG`, specs directory helpers, and config types from `../core/config.js`. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. BOUNDARIES\n\nNon-core scripts should import config through this folder. The canonical config implementation remains in `scripts/core/config.ts`.\n\nAllowed direction:\n\n```text\nextractors/renderers/loaders -> scripts/config -> scripts/core/config\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. VALIDATION\n\nRun the relevant TypeScript or package test command from the repository root after changing exports.\n\n---\n\n## 6. RELATED\n\n- `../core/config.ts`\n- `../graph/README.md`\n- `../observability/README.md`","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":63,"totalLines":63,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/config/README.md","time":{"start":1788625214864,"end":1788625214897}},"id":"prt_0725edd8d001iFNWqJQHU76u6U","sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","messageID":"msg_0725e6df90015NzU5Sme7JsUYf"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788625214907,"sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_hKH6DFWrMxzSyAUQJLKgZPBw","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/resource-map/README.md","offset":1,"limit":100},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/resource-map/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Resource Map Scripts\n2: \n3: > CommonJS helper for turning review or research evidence into a resource map ledger.\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n8: \n9: `scripts/resource-map/` owns the CommonJS helper that turns deep review or deep research evidence into a `resource-map.md` ledger.\n10: \n11: Current state:\n12: \n13: - `extract-from-evidence.cjs` exports `emitResourceMap`.\n14: - The helper accepts review and research evidence shapes.\n15: - Output is a markdown resource ledger grouped by repo file category.\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## 2. OWNERSHIP\n20: \n21: This directory belongs to the System Spec Kit script layer. Keep it usable from CommonJS callers and avoid runtime dependencies that complicate script execution.\n22: \n23: ---\n24: \n25: ## 3. TREE AND KEY FILES\n26: \n27: ```text\n28: scripts/resource-map/\n29: +-- README.md\n30: `-- extract-from-evidence.cjs\n31: ```\n32: \n33: | File | Role |\n34: |---|---|\n35: | `extract-from-evidence.cjs` | Exports `emitResourceMap({ shape, deltas, packet, scope, createdAt })` |\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 4. BOUNDARIES\n40: \n41: - Accept only `review` and `research` shapes unless callers are updated first.\n42: - Emit repo-relative paths only.\n43: - Reject traversal-style paths during normalization.\n44: - Keep category output deterministic.\n45: \n46: ---\n47: \n48: ## 5. VALIDATION\n49: \n50: ```bash\n51: node - <<'NODE'\n52: const { emitResourceMap } = require('./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/resource-map/extract-from-evidence.cjs')\n53: console.log(emitResourceMap({ shape: 'research', deltas: [{ sources: ['README.md'] }], scope: 'smoke' }).includes('README.md'))\n54: NODE\n55: ```\n56: \n57: Expected result: `true`.\n58: \n59: ---\n60: \n61: ## 6. RELATED\n62: \n63: - [`../`](../) - System Spec Kit scripts.\n64: - [`../../templates/level_contract_optional_resource-map.md`](../../templates/addons/resource-map.md.tmpl) - Optional resource map contract.\n\n(End of file - total 64 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Resource Map Scripts\n\n> CommonJS helper for turning review or research evidence into a resource map ledger.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/resource-map/` owns the CommonJS helper that turns deep review or deep research evidence into a `resource-map.md` ledger.\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- `extract-from-evidence.cjs` exports `emitResourceMap`.\n- The helper accepts review and research evidence shapes.\n- Output is a markdown resource ledger grouped by repo file category.\n\n---\n\n## 2. OWNERSHIP\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/resource-map/README.md","text":"# Resource Map Scripts\n\n> CommonJS helper for turning review or research evidence into a resource map ledger.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/resource-map/` owns the CommonJS helper that turns deep review or deep research evidence into a `resource-map.md` ledger.\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- `extract-from-evidence.cjs` exports `emitResourceMap`.\n- The helper accepts review and research evidence shapes.\n- Output is a markdown resource ledger grouped by repo file category.\n\n---\n\n## 2. OWNERSHIP\n\nThis directory belongs to the System Spec Kit script layer. Keep it usable from CommonJS callers and avoid runtime dependencies that complicate script execution.\n\n---\n\n## 3. TREE AND KEY FILES\n\n```text\nscripts/resource-map/\n+-- README.md\n`-- extract-from-evidence.cjs\n```\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| `extract-from-evidence.cjs` | Exports `emitResourceMap({ shape, deltas, packet, scope, createdAt })` |\n\n---\n\n## 4. BOUNDARIES\n\n- Accept only `review` and `research` shapes unless callers are updated first.\n- Emit repo-relative paths only.\n- Reject traversal-style paths during normalization.\n- Keep category output deterministic.\n\n---\n\n## 5. VALIDATION\n\n```bash\nnode - <<'NODE'\nconst { emitResourceMap } = require('./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/resource-map/extract-from-evidence.cjs')\nconsole.log(emitResourceMap({ shape: 'research', deltas: [{ sources: ['README.md'] }], scope: 'smoke' }).includes('README.md'))\nNODE\n```\n\nExpected result: `true`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. RELATED\n\n- [`../`](../) - System Spec Kit scripts.\n- [`../../templates/level_contract_optional_resource-map.md`](../../templates/addons/resource-map.md.tmpl) - Optional resource map contract.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":64,"totalLines":64,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/resource-map/README.md","time":{"start":1788625214870,"end":1788625214898}},"id":"prt_0725edd95001vaj08NwzVkurwt","sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","messageID":"msg_0725e6df90015NzU5Sme7JsUYf"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788625214907,"sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_kdXEXAFxVKLy3jMK7f11lKdJ","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/sweep/README.md","offset":1,"limit":100},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/sweep/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Sweep: strict-pass freshness regression gate\"\n3: description: \"Runs validate.sh --strict across every spec folder and flags regressions against a stored baseline of prior passes.\"\n4: ---\n5: \n6: # Sweep\n7: \n8: ---\n9: \n10: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n11: \n12: `scripts/sweep/` holds the strict-pass freshness sweep, a CI gate that walks every spec folder under `specs` (and legacy `.opencode/specs`), runs `scripts/spec/validate.sh --strict` on each and classifies the result against a prior baseline. A folder that failed with no baseline record is `first-run`, not a regression. A folder that passed before and fails now is a `regression`. This distinguishes genuinely new breakage from a folder that was already failing.\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: ## 2. CONTENTS\n17: \n18: | File | Purpose |\n19: |------|---------|\n20: | `strict-pass-freshness.ts` | CLI entrypoint. `--roots <path[,path...]>` scopes the sweep, `--baseline <report.json>` supplies the prior-pass set, `--format json\\|text` controls output. Classifies each folder as `pass`, `regression`, `new-failure`, `first-run` or `error`. |\n21: \n22: ---\n23: \n24: ## 3. CONSUMERS\n25: \n26: - `.github/workflows/strict-pass-freshness-report.yml` runs this script weekly and reports.\n27:   It does not gate. Merge-blocking lives in `changed-packet-validation.yml`, which is\n28:   scoped to the packets a pull request changed; this sweep exists for the case that gate\n29:   cannot see — a toolchain change breaking packets no pull request touched.\n30: - `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/lib/status-classifier.sh` shares the same pass/fail classification vocabulary.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 4. VALIDATION\n35: \n36: ```bash\n37: npx vitest run .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/strict-pass-freshness.vitest.ts\n38: npx vitest run .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/validation-gate-hardening.vitest.ts\n39: ```\n40: \n41: ---\n42: \n43: ## 5. RELATED\n44: \n45: - [`../spec/validate.sh`](../spec/validate.sh): the per-folder validator this sweep drives.\n46: - [`ENV-REFERENCE.md`](../../runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md): documents the sweep's environment-driven configuration.\n\n(End of file - total 46 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Sweep: strict-pass freshness regression gate\"\ndescription: \"Runs validate.sh --strict across every spec folder and flags regressions against a stored baseline of prior passes.\"\n---\n\n# Sweep\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/sweep/` holds the strict-pass freshness sweep, a CI gate that walks every spec folder under `specs` (and legacy `.opencode/specs`), runs `scripts/spec/validate.sh --strict` on each and classifies the result against a prior baseline. A folder that failed with no baseline record is `first-run`, not a regression. A folder that passed before and fails now is a `regression`. This distinguishes genuinely new breakage from a folder that was already failing.\n\n---\n\n## 2. CONTENTS\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `strict-pass-freshness.ts` | CLI entrypoint. `--roots <path[,path...]>` scopes the sweep, `--baseline <report.json>` supplies the prior-pass set, `--format json\\|text` controls output. Classifies each folder as `pass`, `regression`, `new-failure`, `first-run` or `error`. |","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/sweep/README.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Sweep: strict-pass freshness regression gate\"\ndescription: \"Runs validate.sh --strict across every spec folder and flags regressions against a stored baseline of prior passes.\"\n---\n\n# Sweep\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/sweep/` holds the strict-pass freshness sweep, a CI gate that walks every spec folder under `specs` (and legacy `.opencode/specs`), runs `scripts/spec/validate.sh --strict` on each and classifies the result against a prior baseline. A folder that failed with no baseline record is `first-run`, not a regression. A folder that passed before and fails now is a `regression`. This distinguishes genuinely new breakage from a folder that was already failing.\n\n---\n\n## 2. CONTENTS\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `strict-pass-freshness.ts` | CLI entrypoint. `--roots <path[,path...]>` scopes the sweep, `--baseline <report.json>` supplies the prior-pass set, `--format json\\|text` controls output. Classifies each folder as `pass`, `regression`, `new-failure`, `first-run` or `error`. |\n\n---\n\n## 3. CONSUMERS\n\n- `.github/workflows/strict-pass-freshness-report.yml` runs this script weekly and reports.\n  It does not gate. Merge-blocking lives in `changed-packet-validation.yml`, which is\n  scoped to the packets a pull request changed; this sweep exists for the case that gate\n  cannot see — a toolchain change breaking packets no pull request touched.\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/lib/status-classifier.sh` shares the same pass/fail classification vocabulary.\n\n---\n\n## 4. VALIDATION\n\n```bash\nnpx vitest run .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/strict-pass-freshness.vitest.ts\nnpx vitest run .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/validation-gate-hardening.vitest.ts\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. RELATED\n\n- [`../spec/validate.sh`](../spec/validate.sh): the per-folder validator this sweep drives.\n- [`ENV-REFERENCE.md`](../../runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md): documents the sweep's environment-driven configuration.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":46,"totalLines":46,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/sweep/README.md","time":{"start":1788625214878,"end":1788625214898}},"id":"prt_0725edd9d001VMwV3Z5Mf3DxeE","sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","messageID":"msg_0725e6df90015NzU5Sme7JsUYf"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788625214907,"sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_uclaCcEwVVfJcKW0i5aEMVeT","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/ops/README.md","offset":1,"limit":110},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/ops/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Ops Self-Healing Scripts\"\n3: description: \"Deterministic runbook helpers for spec-kit operational failure classes with bounded retry and escalation output.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"ops runbook\"\n6:   - \"self-healing scripts\"\n7:   - \"index drift remediation\"\n8:   - \"telemetry drift drill\"\n9: ---\n10: \n11: # Ops Self-Healing Scripts\n12: \n13: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n14: \n15: `scripts/ops/` contains deterministic shell runbooks for known spec-kit operational failure classes. `runbook.sh` still lists and dispatches to both registered failure classes, but neither `heal-*.sh` script currently completes a detect/repair/verify cycle: `heal-session-ambiguity.sh` is a deprecated stub that logs a deprecation notice and exits before running any step, and `heal-telemetry-drift.sh` parses and validates its options but always reports that its verifier was removed and exits with an error. Both wait on a replacement remediation path.\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## 2. SCRIPT IO\n20: \n21: | Flow | Input | Output |\n22: | --- | --- | --- |\n23: | Class listing | `runbook.sh list` | Supported failure class keys |\n24: | Runbook detail | `runbook.sh show <class>` | Human-readable runbook for one class |\n25: | Drill execution | `runbook.sh drill <class|all> --scenario <success|escalate>` | Deprecation notice (`session-ambiguity`, exit 0) or a removed-verifier error (`telemetry-drift`, exit 1) |\n26: | Healer execution | Failure class plus retry options | Currently a deprecation stub or a removed-verifier error, not a live detect/repair/verify sequence |\n27: \n28: Registered classes are `session-ambiguity` and `telemetry-drift`; both healers are stubs pending a replacement remediation path (see Overview).\n29: \n30: ---\n31: \n32: ## 3. ENTRYPOINTS\n33: \n34: - `runbook.sh list` prints supported failure classes.\n35: - `runbook.sh show <class>` prints one class runbook.\n36: - `runbook.sh drill <class|all> --scenario <success|escalate> --max-attempts <n>` runs bounded remediation drills.\n37: - `heal-*.sh` scripts hold the class-specific detect, repair, and verify flow structure, but each currently stops before completing a cycle (see Overview).\n38: - `ops-common.sh` provides shared retry, logging, and escalation helpers.\n39: - `process-memory-harness.ts` captures process/RSS/swap/wired snapshots used by arc 009 memory evidence.\n40: - `process-sweep.ts` emits dry-run plans and an `apply` result. No terminable process class is registered, so `apply` signals nothing and reports `no-terminable-class-registered`; termination returns only when a class is registered together with the ownership evidence that proves the process is this repository's to kill.\n41: \n42: ---\n43: \n44: ## 4. VALIDATION FROM REPO ROOT\n45: \n46: Run ops validation from the repository root:\n47: \n48: ```bash\n49: bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/ops/runbook.sh list\n50: bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/ops/runbook.sh show session-ambiguity\n51: bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/ops/runbook.sh drill all --scenario success --max-attempts 1\n52: python3 .opencode/skills/sk-code/sk-code-opencode/assets/scripts/verify_alignment_drift.py --root .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/ops\n53: ```\n54: \n55: ---\n56: \n57: ## 5. KEY FILES\n58: \n59: | File | Purpose |\n60: | --- | --- |\n61: | `ops-common.sh` | Shared retry, logging, option parsing, and escalation helpers |\n62: | `heal-session-ambiguity.sh` | Deprecated stub: logs a deprecation notice and exits 0 before the retained (unreachable) detect/repair logic runs. Session ambiguity is now handled by the memory-save pipeline (`generate-context.js`). |\n63: | `heal-telemetry-drift.sh` | Parses and validates its options, then always reports that its telemetry-drift verifier was removed and exits 1. No replacement verifier is wired yet. |\n64: | `runbook.sh` | Class listing, runbook display, and drill orchestration |\n65: | `process-memory-harness.ts` | Process inventory, memory snapshot and exact-identity classification helper |\n66: | `process-sweep.ts` | Dry-run planner plus a report-only apply path; it signals nothing while no terminable class is registered |\n67: \n68: Arc 009 lifecycle helper map:\n69: \n70: | Surface | Helper |\n71: | --- | --- |\n72: | Deep loop runtime | `runtime//lib/deep-loop/loop-lock.ts`, `jsonl-repair.ts`, `atomic-state.ts` |\n73: | Spec Kit runtime | `runtime/lib/memory/bounded-cache.ts`, `audit-rotation.ts`, `runtime/lib/runtime/timer-registry.ts`, `shutdown-hooks.ts` |\n74: | Ops | `scripts/ops/process-memory-harness.ts`, `scripts/ops/process-sweep.ts` |\n75: \n76: ---\n77: \n78: ## 6. BOUNDARIES\n79: \n80: - Ops scripts model known failure classes; they are not a general incident-management system.\n81: - Healers must keep bounded retries and emit one escalation JSON line on retry exhaustion.\n82: - Scripts should remain deterministic so drills and release gates are repeatable.\n83: \n84: ---\n85: \n86: ## 7. RELATED\n87: \n88: - `../README.md`\n89: - `../spec/README.md`\n90: - `../../runtime/README.md`\n\n(End of file - total 90 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Ops Self-Healing Scripts\"\ndescription: \"Deterministic runbook helpers for spec-kit operational failure classes with bounded retry and escalation output.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"ops runbook\"\n  - \"self-healing scripts\"\n  - \"index drift remediation\"\n  - \"telemetry drift drill\"\n---\n\n# Ops Self-Healing Scripts\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/ops/` contains deterministic shell runbooks for known spec-kit operational failure classes. `runbook.sh` still lists and dispatches to both registered failure classes, but neither `heal-*.sh` script currently completes a detect/repair/verify cycle: `heal-session-ambiguity.sh` is a deprecated stub that logs a deprecation notice and exits before running any step, and `heal-telemetry-drift.sh` parses and validates its options but always reports that its verifier was removed and exits with an error. Both wait on a replacement remediation path.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SCRIPT IO\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/ops/README.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Ops Self-Healing Scripts\"\ndescription: \"Deterministic runbook helpers for spec-kit operational failure classes with bounded retry and escalation output.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"ops runbook\"\n  - \"self-healing scripts\"\n  - \"index drift remediation\"\n  - \"telemetry drift drill\"\n---\n\n# Ops Self-Healing Scripts\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/ops/` contains deterministic shell runbooks for known spec-kit operational failure classes. `runbook.sh` still lists and dispatches to both registered failure classes, but neither `heal-*.sh` script currently completes a detect/repair/verify cycle: `heal-session-ambiguity.sh` is a deprecated stub that logs a deprecation notice and exits before running any step, and `heal-telemetry-drift.sh` parses and validates its options but always reports that its verifier was removed and exits with an error. Both wait on a replacement remediation path.\n\n---\n\n## 2. SCRIPT IO\n\n| Flow | Input | Output |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Class listing | `runbook.sh list` | Supported failure class keys |\n| Runbook detail | `runbook.sh show <class>` | Human-readable runbook for one class |\n| Drill execution | `runbook.sh drill <class|all> --scenario <success|escalate>` | Deprecation notice (`session-ambiguity`, exit 0) or a removed-verifier error (`telemetry-drift`, exit 1) |\n| Healer execution | Failure class plus retry options | Currently a deprecation stub or a removed-verifier error, not a live detect/repair/verify sequence |\n\nRegistered classes are `session-ambiguity` and `telemetry-drift`; both healers are stubs pending a replacement remediation path (see Overview).\n\n---\n\n## 3. ENTRYPOINTS\n\n- `runbook.sh list` prints supported failure classes.\n- `runbook.sh show <class>` prints one class runbook.\n- `runbook.sh drill <class|all> --scenario <success|escalate> --max-attempts <n>` runs bounded remediation drills.\n- `heal-*.sh` scripts hold the class-specific detect, repair, and verify flow structure, but each currently stops before completing a cycle (see Overview).\n- `ops-common.sh` provides shared retry, logging, and escalation helpers.\n- `process-memory-harness.ts` captures process/RSS/swap/wired snapshots used by arc 009 memory evidence.\n- `process-sweep.ts` emits dry-run plans and an `apply` result. No terminable process class is registered, so `apply` signals nothing and reports `no-terminable-class-registered`; termination returns only when a class is registered together with the ownership evidence that proves the process is this repository's to kill.\n\n---\n\n## 4. VALIDATION FROM REPO ROOT\n\nRun ops validation from the repository root:\n\n```bash\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/ops/runbook.sh list\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/ops/runbook.sh show session-ambiguity\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/ops/runbook.sh drill all --scenario success --max-attempts 1\npython3 .opencode/skills/sk-code/sk-code-opencode/assets/scripts/verify_alignment_drift.py --root .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/ops\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `ops-common.sh` | Shared retry, logging, option parsing, and escalation helpers |\n| `heal-session-ambiguity.sh` | Deprecated stub: logs a deprecation notice and exits 0 before the retained (unreachable) detect/repair logic runs. Session ambiguity is now handled by the memory-save pipeline (`generate-context.js`). |\n| `heal-telemetry-drift.sh` | Parses and validates its options, then always reports that its telemetry-drift verifier was removed and exits 1. No replacement verifier is wired yet. |\n| `runbook.sh` | Class listing, runbook display, and drill orchestration |\n| `process-memory-harness.ts` | Process inventory, memory snapshot and exact-identity classification helper |\n| `process-sweep.ts` | Dry-run planner plus a report-only apply path; it signals nothing while no terminable class is registered |\n\nArc 009 lifecycle helper map:\n\n| Surface | Helper |\n| --- | --- |\n| Deep loop runtime | `runtime//lib/deep-loop/loop-lock.ts`, `jsonl-repair.ts`, `atomic-state.ts` |\n| Spec Kit runtime | `runtime/lib/memory/bounded-cache.ts`, `audit-rotation.ts`, `runtime/lib/runtime/timer-registry.ts`, `shutdown-hooks.ts` |\n| Ops | `scripts/ops/process-memory-harness.ts`, `scripts/ops/process-sweep.ts` |\n\n---\n\n## 6. BOUNDARIES\n\n- Ops scripts model known failure classes; they are not a general incident-management system.\n- Healers must keep bounded retries and emit one escalation JSON line on retry exhaustion.\n- Scripts should remain deterministic so drills and release gates are repeatable.\n\n---\n\n## 7. RELATED\n\n- `../README.md`\n- `../spec/README.md`\n- `../../runtime/README.md`","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":90,"totalLines":90,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/ops/README.md","time":{"start":1788625214877,"end":1788625214899}},"id":"prt_0725edd9b001fuK3cxW4egOerY","sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","messageID":"msg_0725e6df90015NzU5Sme7JsUYf"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788625214907,"sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_9g9GMWJ3RlzKOlOHA5ZbxZ2k","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/test-validation.sh","offset":1,"limit":80},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/test-validation.sh</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: #!/usr/bin/env bash\n2: # ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n3: # COMPONENT: Legacy Validation Test Wrapper\n4: # ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n5: # Backward-compatible entrypoint forwarding to cli/tests.\n6: \n7: set -euo pipefail\n8: \n9: SCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\n10: exec \"${SCRIPT_DIR}/../tests/test-validation.sh\" \"$@\"\n11: \n12: # Exit codes:\n13: #   0 - Success\n\n(End of file - total 13 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# COMPONENT: Legacy Validation Test Wrapper\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Backward-compatible entrypoint forwarding to cli/tests.\n\nset -euo pipefail\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\nexec \"${SCRIPT_DIR}/../tests/test-validation.sh\" \"$@\"\n\n# Exit codes:\n#   0 - Success","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/test-validation.sh","text":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# COMPONENT: Legacy Validation Test Wrapper\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# Backward-compatible entrypoint forwarding to cli/tests.\n\nset -euo pipefail\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\nexec \"${SCRIPT_DIR}/../tests/test-validation.sh\" \"$@\"\n\n# Exit codes:\n#   0 - Success","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":13,"totalLines":13,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/test-validation.sh","time":{"start":1788625214887,"end":1788625214900}},"id":"prt_0725edda60014op58hJf7eX5gB","sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","messageID":"msg_0725e6df90015NzU5Sme7JsUYf"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788625214907,"sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_i5NUpxWK3ADSQ6bcF0cTd3Pu","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/directory-setup.ts","offset":1,"limit":130},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/directory-setup.ts</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // MODULE: Directory Setup\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: \n5: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n6: // 1. DIRECTORY SETUP\n7: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n8: // Validates that the target spec folder exists and is usable\n9: \n10: // Node stdlib\n11: import * as fs from 'fs/promises';\n12: import * as path from 'path';\n13: \n14: // Internal modules\n15: import { structuredLog, sanitizePath } from '../utils/index.js';\n16: import { CONFIG, findActiveSpecsDir, getSpecsDirectories, SPEC_FOLDER_PATTERN } from '../core/index.js';\n17: \n18: /* ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n19:    1. DIRECTORY SETUP\n20: ------------------------------------------------------------------*/\n21: \n22: async function ensureSpecFolderExists(specFolder: string): Promise<string> {\n23:   let sanitizedPath: string;\n24:   try {\n25:     sanitizedPath = sanitizePath(specFolder, getSpecsDirectories());\n26:   } catch (sanitizeError: unknown) {\n27:     const errMsg = sanitizeError instanceof Error ? sanitizeError.message : String(sanitizeError);\n28:     structuredLog('error', 'Invalid spec folder path', {\n29:       specFolder,\n30:       error: errMsg\n31:     });\n32:     throw new Error(`Invalid spec folder path: ${errMsg}`);\n33:   }\n34: \n35:   const leafFolder = path.basename(sanitizedPath);\n36:   if (!SPEC_FOLDER_PATTERN.test(leafFolder)) {\n37:     structuredLog('error', 'Spec folder leaf name is invalid', {\n38:       specFolder: sanitizedPath,\n39:       expected: 'NNN-name'\n40:     });\n41:     throw new Error(\n42:       `Invalid spec folder path: expected leaf folder in NNN-name format, received \"${leafFolder}\"`\n43:     );\n44:   }\n45: \n46:   try {\n47:     const stats = await fs.stat(sanitizedPath);\n48:     if (!stats.isDirectory()) {\n49:       throw new Error(`Path exists but is not a directory: ${sanitizedPath}`);\n50:     }\n51:   } catch (err: unknown) {\n52:     const nodeErr = err instanceof Error ? (err as NodeJS.ErrnoException) : undefined;\n53:     if (nodeErr?.code === 'ENOENT') {\n54:       const specsDir = findActiveSpecsDir() || path.join(CONFIG.PROJECT_ROOT, 'specs');\n55:       let availableFolders: string[] = [];\n56:       try {\n57:         const entries = await fs.readdir(specsDir, { withFileTypes: true });\n58:         availableFolders = entries\n59:           .filter((e) => e.isDirectory())\n60:           .map((e) => e.name)\n61:           .slice(0, 10);\n62:       } catch (error: unknown) {\n63:         if (error instanceof Error) {\n64:           // Specs/ doesn't exist or can't be read\n65:         }\n66:       }\n67: \n68:       let errorMsg = `Spec folder does not exist: ${sanitizedPath}`;\n69:       errorMsg += '\\nPlease create the spec folder first or check the path.';\n70:       errorMsg += `\\nSearched in: ${getSpecsDirectories().join(', ')}`;\n71:       if (availableFolders.length > 0) {\n72:         const activeDirName = path.basename(specsDir);\n73:         errorMsg += `\\n\\nAvailable spec folders (in ${activeDirName}/):`;\n74:         availableFolders.forEach((f) => errorMsg += `\\n  - ${activeDirName}/${f}`);\n75:       }\n76:       structuredLog('error', 'Spec folder not found', {\n77:         specFolder: sanitizedPath,\n78:         availableFolders\n79:       });\n80:       throw new Error(errorMsg);\n81:     }\n82:     throw err;\n83:   }\n84: \n85:   return sanitizedPath;\n86: }\n87: \n88: /* ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n89:    2. EXPORTS\n90: ------------------------------------------------------------------*/\n91: \n92: export {\n93:   ensureSpecFolderExists,\n94: };\n\n(End of file - total 94 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// MODULE: Directory Setup\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. DIRECTORY SETUP\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// Validates that the target spec folder exists and is usable\n\n// Node stdlib\nimport * as fs from 'fs/promises';\nimport * as path from 'path';\n\n// Internal modules\nimport { structuredLog, sanitizePath } from '../utils/index.js';\nimport { CONFIG, findActiveSpecsDir, getSpecsDirectories, SPEC_FOLDER_PATTERN } from '../core/index.js';\n\n/* ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n   1. DIRECTORY SETUP\n------------------------------------------------------------------*/","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/directory-setup.ts","text":"// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// MODULE: Directory Setup\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. DIRECTORY SETUP\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// Validates that the target spec folder exists and is usable\n\n// Node stdlib\nimport * as fs from 'fs/promises';\nimport * as path from 'path';\n\n// Internal modules\nimport { structuredLog, sanitizePath } from '../utils/index.js';\nimport { CONFIG, findActiveSpecsDir, getSpecsDirectories, SPEC_FOLDER_PATTERN } from '../core/index.js';\n\n/* ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n   1. DIRECTORY SETUP\n------------------------------------------------------------------*/\n\nasync function ensureSpecFolderExists(specFolder: string): Promise<string> {\n  let sanitizedPath: string;\n  try {\n    sanitizedPath = sanitizePath(specFolder, getSpecsDirectories());\n  } catch (sanitizeError: unknown) {\n    const errMsg = sanitizeError instanceof Error ? sanitizeError.message : String(sanitizeError);\n    structuredLog('error', 'Invalid spec folder path', {\n      specFolder,\n      error: errMsg\n    });\n    throw new Error(`Invalid spec folder path: ${errMsg}`);\n  }\n\n  const leafFolder = path.basename(sanitizedPath);\n  if (!SPEC_FOLDER_PATTERN.test(leafFolder)) {\n    structuredLog('error', 'Spec folder leaf name is invalid', {\n      specFolder: sanitizedPath,\n      expected: 'NNN-name'\n    });\n    throw new Error(\n      `Invalid spec folder path: expected leaf folder in NNN-name format, received \"${leafFolder}\"`\n    );\n  }\n\n  try {\n    const stats = await fs.stat(sanitizedPath);\n    if (!stats.isDirectory()) {\n      throw new Error(`Path exists but is not a directory: ${sanitizedPath}`);\n    }\n  } catch (err: unknown) {\n    const nodeErr = err instanceof Error ? (err as NodeJS.ErrnoException) : undefined;\n    if (nodeErr?.code === 'ENOENT') {\n      const specsDir = findActiveSpecsDir() || path.join(CONFIG.PROJECT_ROOT, 'specs');\n      let availableFolders: string[] = [];\n      try {\n        const entries = await fs.readdir(specsDir, { withFileTypes: true });\n        availableFolders = entries\n          .filter((e) => e.isDirectory())\n          .map((e) => e.name)\n          .slice(0, 10);\n      } catch (error: unknown) {\n        if (error instanceof Error) {\n          // Specs/ doesn't exist or can't be read\n        }\n      }\n\n      let errorMsg = `Spec folder does not exist: ${sanitizedPath}`;\n      errorMsg += '\\nPlease create the spec folder first or check the path.';\n      errorMsg += `\\nSearched in: ${getSpecsDirectories().join(', ')}`;\n      if (availableFolders.length > 0) {\n        const activeDirName = path.basename(specsDir);\n        errorMsg += `\\n\\nAvailable spec folders (in ${activeDirName}/):`;\n        availableFolders.forEach((f) => errorMsg += `\\n  - ${activeDirName}/${f}`);\n      }\n      structuredLog('error', 'Spec folder not found', {\n        specFolder: sanitizedPath,\n        availableFolders\n      });\n      throw new Error(errorMsg);\n    }\n    throw err;\n  }\n\n  return sanitizedPath;\n}\n\n/* ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n   2. EXPORTS\n------------------------------------------------------------------*/\n\nexport {\n  ensureSpecFolderExists,\n};","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":94,"totalLines":94,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec-folder/directory-setup.ts","time":{"start":1788625214882,"end":1788625214901}},"id":"prt_0725edda1001XPeJ7T99o94Xgs","sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","messageID":"msg_0725e6df90015NzU5Sme7JsUYf"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788625214907,"sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_eWTo4BLhPXXeNpyGRl9EgR1M","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/README.md","offset":1,"limit":120},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"KPI Scripts\"\n3: description: \"Quality KPI reporter for generated continuity support artifacts under spec memory folders.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"quality kpi\"\n6:   - \"memory quality rates\"\n7:   - \"placeholder rate\"\n8:   - \"contamination check\"\n9: ---\n10: \n11: <!-- markdownlint-disable MD025 -->\n12: \n13: # KPI Scripts\n14: \n15: ---\n16: \n17: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n18: \n19: `scripts/kpi/` reports defect rates for generated continuity support\n20: artifacts. It scans markdown under spec `memory/` directories and emits JSON\n21: metrics plus a concise stderr summary.\n22: \n23: Boundary:\n24: \n25: - Resume source of truth remains\n26:   `handover.md -> _memory.continuity -> spec docs`.\n27: - Generated memory artifacts are supporting evidence only.\n28: - Defect rates are reported, not enforced; callers decide thresholds.\n29: \n30: ---\n31: \n32: ## 2. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n33: \n34: ```text\n35: scripts/kpi/\n36: +-- quality-kpi.sh  # Shell wrapper with inline Node.js scanner\n37: `-- README.md\n38: ```\n39: \n40: Flow:\n41: \n42: ```text\n43: quality-kpi.sh -> <active-spec-folder>/**/memory/*.md -> JSON rates + summary\n44: ```\n45: \n46: Metrics:\n47: \n48: | Metric | Flags |\n49: | --- | --- |\n50: | Placeholder rate | `[TBD]`, `[Not assessed]`, `[N/A]` |\n51: | Fallback rate | Generic fallback phrases in generated content |\n52: | Contamination rate | AI process leakage such as \"Let me analyze\" |\n53: | Empty trigger phrase rate | Frontmatter with no `trigger_phrases` entries |\n54: \n55: ---\n56: \n57: ## 3. ENTRYPOINTS\n58: \n59: Run from the repository root:\n60: \n61: ```bash\n62: bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/quality-kpi.sh\n63: bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/quality-kpi.sh \\\n64:   \"system-spec-kit/022-hybrid-rag-fusion\"\n65: ```\n66: \n67: The optional argument is a spec-folder path relative to `specs/`.\n68: \n69: ---\n70: \n71: ## 4. VALIDATION\n72: \n73: Use repository-root commands:\n74: \n75: ```bash\n76: bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/quality-kpi.sh >/tmp/spec-kit-kpi.json\n77: node -e \"const fs=require('fs'); \\\n78: JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/tmp/spec-kit-kpi.json','utf8')); \\\n79: console.log('valid json')\"\n80: ```\n81: \n82: Expected behavior: the first command exits `0`, writes JSON to stdout and\n83: prints a `KPI Summary:` line to stderr.\n84: \n85: ---\n86: \n87: ## 5. RELATED\n88: \n89: - [`../README.md`](../README.md)\n90: - [`../memory/README.md`](../memory/README.md)\n91: - [`../evals/README.md`](../evals/README.md)\n92: - [`../tests/README.md`](../tests/README.md)\n\n(End of file - total 92 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"KPI Scripts\"\ndescription: \"Quality KPI reporter for generated continuity support artifacts under spec memory folders.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"quality kpi\"\n  - \"memory quality rates\"\n  - \"placeholder rate\"\n  - \"contamination check\"\n---\n\n<!-- markdownlint-disable MD025 -->\n\n# KPI Scripts\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/kpi/` reports defect rates for generated continuity support\nartifacts. It scans markdown under spec `memory/` directories and emits JSON","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/README.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"KPI Scripts\"\ndescription: \"Quality KPI reporter for generated continuity support artifacts under spec memory folders.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"quality kpi\"\n  - \"memory quality rates\"\n  - \"placeholder rate\"\n  - \"contamination check\"\n---\n\n<!-- markdownlint-disable MD025 -->\n\n# KPI Scripts\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/kpi/` reports defect rates for generated continuity support\nartifacts. It scans markdown under spec `memory/` directories and emits JSON\nmetrics plus a concise stderr summary.\n\nBoundary:\n\n- Resume source of truth remains\n  `handover.md -> _memory.continuity -> spec docs`.\n- Generated memory artifacts are supporting evidence only.\n- Defect rates are reported, not enforced; callers decide thresholds.\n\n---\n\n## 2. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n\n```text\nscripts/kpi/\n+-- quality-kpi.sh  # Shell wrapper with inline Node.js scanner\n`-- README.md\n```\n\nFlow:\n\n```text\nquality-kpi.sh -> <active-spec-folder>/**/memory/*.md -> JSON rates + summary\n```\n\nMetrics:\n\n| Metric | Flags |\n| --- | --- |\n| Placeholder rate | `[TBD]`, `[Not assessed]`, `[N/A]` |\n| Fallback rate | Generic fallback phrases in generated content |\n| Contamination rate | AI process leakage such as \"Let me analyze\" |\n| Empty trigger phrase rate | Frontmatter with no `trigger_phrases` entries |\n\n---\n\n## 3. ENTRYPOINTS\n\nRun from the repository root:\n\n```bash\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/quality-kpi.sh\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/quality-kpi.sh \\\n  \"system-spec-kit/022-hybrid-rag-fusion\"\n```\n\nThe optional argument is a spec-folder path relative to `specs/`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. VALIDATION\n\nUse repository-root commands:\n\n```bash\nbash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/quality-kpi.sh >/tmp/spec-kit-kpi.json\nnode -e \"const fs=require('fs'); \\\nJSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/tmp/spec-kit-kpi.json','utf8')); \\\nconsole.log('valid json')\"\n```\n\nExpected behavior: the first command exits `0`, writes JSON to stdout and\nprints a `KPI Summary:` line to stderr.\n\n---\n\n## 5. RELATED\n\n- [`../README.md`](../README.md)\n- [`../memory/README.md`](../memory/README.md)\n- [`../evals/README.md`](../evals/README.md)\n- [`../tests/README.md`](../tests/README.md)","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":92,"totalLines":92,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/kpi/README.md","time":{"start":1788625214873,"end":1788625214902}},"id":"prt_0725edd97001g8ED8HzHsi4ANs","sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","messageID":"msg_0725e6df90015NzU5Sme7JsUYf"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788625214907,"sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_QP4Zm9PfeyoODLFwfhCB0K5L","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/evals/README.md","offset":1,"limit":150},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/evals/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Eval Scripts\"\n3: description: \"Import-policy, architecture-boundary, dist-alignment and calibration checks for the Spec Kit engine.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"eval scripts\"\n6:   - \"run benchmarks\"\n7:   - \"import policy\"\n8:   - \"architecture boundaries\"\n9: ---\n10: \n11: # Eval Scripts\n12: \n13: > CLI utilities for policy checks, dist alignment, redaction calibration and scripts-to-runtime boundaries.\n14: \n15: ---\n16: \n17: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n18: \n19: `scripts/evals/` contains policy checks and calibration helpers for the Spec Kit engine. The tools cover import boundaries, handler cycles, source-to-dist alignment, redaction calibration and closure metrics.\n20: \n21: Current state:\n22: \n23: - TypeScript scripts run with `npx tsx` from the scripts workspace; `run-phase2-closure-metrics.mjs` runs with `node`.\n24: - Import policy checks prefer the runtime package's public API (`@spec-kit/runtime/api`) over internal runtime paths.\n25: - Allowlisted exceptions are tracked in `import-policy-allowlist.json`.\n26: - The retrieval-quality runners that used to live here — `run-ablation.ts`, `run-bm25-baseline.ts` and `run-performance-benchmarks.ts` — were removed with the memory engine, along with `map-ground-truth-ids.ts`. Nothing replaced them, because the search pipeline they measured no longer exists.\n27: \n28: ---\n29: \n30: ## 2. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n31: \n32: ```text\n33: scripts/evals/\n34: +-- check-allowlist-expiry.ts                 # Import exception expiry checks\n35: +-- check-architecture-boundaries.ts          # Architecture boundary checks\n36: +-- check-handler-cycles-ast.ts               # Handler cycle detection\n37: +-- check-no-mcp-lib-imports.ts               # Internal runtime import checks\n38: +-- check-no-mcp-lib-imports-ast.ts           # AST variant of the same check\n39: +-- check-source-dist-alignment.ts            # Orphaned dist artifact detection\n40: +-- collect-redaction-calibration-inputs.ts   # Redaction calibration inputs\n41: +-- run-redaction-calibration.ts              # Redaction threshold calibration\n42: +-- run-phase2-closure-metrics.mjs            # Closure metrics into a spec folder's scratch/\n43: +-- import-policy-rules.ts                    # Shared import policy rules\n44: +-- import-policy-allowlist.json              # Managed import exceptions\n45: `-- README.md\n46: ```\n47: \n48: Allowed import surfaces:\n49: \n50: - `../../runtime/api`\n51: - `../../runtime/api/*`\n52: - `../../shared/`\n53: \n54: Restricted import surfaces:\n55: \n56: - `@spec-kit/runtime/lib*`\n57: - `@spec-kit/runtime/core*`\n58: - `@spec-kit/runtime/handlers*`\n59: - Relative imports into `../../runtime/{lib,core,handlers}`\n60: \n61: ---\n62: \n63: ## 3. KEY FILES\n64: \n65: | File | Responsibility |\n66: |---|---|\n67: | `check-no-mcp-lib-imports-ast.ts` | Enforces restricted import policy with AST traversal. |\n68: | `check-no-mcp-lib-imports.ts` | Text-scan variant of the same restricted import policy. |\n69: | `check-allowlist-expiry.ts` | Warns on near-expiry import exceptions and fails on expired ones. |\n70: | `check-architecture-boundaries.ts` | Checks shared neutrality and wrapper-only boundaries. |\n71: | `check-handler-cycles-ast.ts` | Detects import cycles between handlers. |\n72: | `check-source-dist-alignment.ts` | Maps each runtime-critical `dist/**/*.js` back to its source `.ts` and flags orphans left by deleted or renamed sources. |\n73: | `run-redaction-calibration.ts` | Calibrates sensitive-content redaction thresholds. |\n74: | `collect-redaction-calibration-inputs.ts` | Collects data used by redaction calibration runs. |\n75: | `run-phase2-closure-metrics.mjs` | Generates closure metrics for a named spec folder and writes them under that folder's `scratch/`. Takes the spec-folder path as its one argument. |\n76: | `import-policy-rules.ts` | Shared rule definitions used by the import policy checks. |\n77: | `import-policy-allowlist.json` | Stores temporary approved exceptions with owner and expiry metadata. |\n78: \n79: ---\n80: \n81: ## 4. COMMANDS\n82: \n83: Run from `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli` unless a command uses a repository-root path.\n84: \n85: ```bash\n86: npx tsx evals/check-no-mcp-lib-imports-ast.ts\n87: ```\n88: \n89: Expected result: exits zero when eval scripts avoid restricted runtime imports or use valid allowlist entries.\n90: \n91: ```bash\n92: npx tsx evals/check-allowlist-expiry.ts\n93: ```\n94: \n95: Expected result: warns on near-expiry exceptions and fails on expired exceptions.\n96: \n97: ```bash\n98: npx tsx evals/check-source-dist-alignment.ts\n99: ```\n100: \n101: Expected result: exits zero when every runtime-critical dist artifact still has a matching source file, and reports a violation for each orphan left by a deleted or renamed source.\n102: \n103: ```bash\n104: node evals/run-phase2-closure-metrics.mjs specs/<track>/<packet>\n105: ```\n106: \n107: Expected result: writes closure metrics into that spec folder's `scratch/` directory. Without the spec-folder argument it exits with a usage error.\n108: \n109: ---\n110: \n111: ## 5. BOUNDARIES\n112: \n113: | Boundary | Rule |\n114: |---|---|\n115: | Public API | Eval scripts should use the runtime package's public API (`@spec-kit/runtime/api`) rather than internal runtime modules. |\n116: | Exceptions | Internal runtime access requires an allowlist entry with owner, reason and expiry. |\n117: | Data | Calibration and metrics scripts may read fixtures and write into a named spec folder's `scratch/`, but should not rewrite tracked artifacts unless a command documents that behavior. |\n118: | Reporting | Output should state when prerequisites are missing or results are investigation-only. |\n119: \n120: ---\n121: \n122: ## 6. VALIDATION\n123: \n124: Run the README validator after editing this file:\n125: \n126: ```bash\n127: python3 .opencode/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/evals/README.md\n128: ```\n129: \n130: Run policy checks after changing eval scripts:\n131: \n132: ```bash\n133: cd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli\n134: npx tsx evals/check-no-mcp-lib-imports-ast.ts\n135: npx tsx evals/check-allowlist-expiry.ts\n136: ```\n137: \n138: Expected result: both policy checks exit zero or report a documented exception that needs review.\n139: \n140: ---\n141: \n142: ## 7. RELATED\n143: \n144: - [`../README.md`](../README.md)\n145: - [`../core/README.md`](../core/README.md)\n146: - [`../../ARCHITECTURE.md`](../../ARCHITECTURE.md)\n147: - [`import-policy-allowlist.json`](./import-policy-allowlist.json)\n\n(End of file - total 147 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Eval Scripts\"\ndescription: \"Import-policy, architecture-boundary, dist-alignment and calibration checks for the Spec Kit engine.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"eval scripts\"\n  - \"run benchmarks\"\n  - \"import policy\"\n  - \"architecture boundaries\"\n---\n\n# Eval Scripts\n\n> CLI utilities for policy checks, dist alignment, redaction calibration and scripts-to-runtime boundaries.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/evals/` contains policy checks and calibration helpers for the Spec Kit engine. The tools cover import boundaries, handler cycles, source-to-dist alignment, redaction calibration and closure metrics.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/evals/README.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Eval Scripts\"\ndescription: \"Import-policy, architecture-boundary, dist-alignment and calibration checks for the Spec Kit engine.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"eval scripts\"\n  - \"run benchmarks\"\n  - \"import policy\"\n  - \"architecture boundaries\"\n---\n\n# Eval Scripts\n\n> CLI utilities for policy checks, dist alignment, redaction calibration and scripts-to-runtime boundaries.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/evals/` contains policy checks and calibration helpers for the Spec Kit engine. The tools cover import boundaries, handler cycles, source-to-dist alignment, redaction calibration and closure metrics.\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- TypeScript scripts run with `npx tsx` from the scripts workspace; `run-phase2-closure-metrics.mjs` runs with `node`.\n- Import policy checks prefer the runtime package's public API (`@spec-kit/runtime/api`) over internal runtime paths.\n- Allowlisted exceptions are tracked in `import-policy-allowlist.json`.\n- The retrieval-quality runners that used to live here — `run-ablation.ts`, `run-bm25-baseline.ts` and `run-performance-benchmarks.ts` — were removed with the memory engine, along with `map-ground-truth-ids.ts`. Nothing replaced them, because the search pipeline they measured no longer exists.\n\n---\n\n## 2. PACKAGE TOPOLOGY\n\n```text\nscripts/evals/\n+-- check-allowlist-expiry.ts                 # Import exception expiry checks\n+-- check-architecture-boundaries.ts          # Architecture boundary checks\n+-- check-handler-cycles-ast.ts               # Handler cycle detection\n+-- check-no-mcp-lib-imports.ts               # Internal runtime import checks\n+-- check-no-mcp-lib-imports-ast.ts           # AST variant of the same check\n+-- check-source-dist-alignment.ts            # Orphaned dist artifact detection\n+-- collect-redaction-calibration-inputs.ts   # Redaction calibration inputs\n+-- run-redaction-calibration.ts              # Redaction threshold calibration\n+-- run-phase2-closure-metrics.mjs            # Closure metrics into a spec folder's scratch/\n+-- import-policy-rules.ts                    # Shared import policy rules\n+-- import-policy-allowlist.json              # Managed import exceptions\n`-- README.md\n```\n\nAllowed import surfaces:\n\n- `../../runtime/api`\n- `../../runtime/api/*`\n- `../../shared/`\n\nRestricted import surfaces:\n\n- `@spec-kit/runtime/lib*`\n- `@spec-kit/runtime/core*`\n- `@spec-kit/runtime/handlers*`\n- Relative imports into `../../runtime/{lib,core,handlers}`\n\n---\n\n## 3. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `check-no-mcp-lib-imports-ast.ts` | Enforces restricted import policy with AST traversal. |\n| `check-no-mcp-lib-imports.ts` | Text-scan variant of the same restricted import policy. |\n| `check-allowlist-expiry.ts` | Warns on near-expiry import exceptions and fails on expired ones. |\n| `check-architecture-boundaries.ts` | Checks shared neutrality and wrapper-only boundaries. |\n| `check-handler-cycles-ast.ts` | Detects import cycles between handlers. |\n| `check-source-dist-alignment.ts` | Maps each runtime-critical `dist/**/*.js` back to its source `.ts` and flags orphans left by deleted or renamed sources. |\n| `run-redaction-calibration.ts` | Calibrates sensitive-content redaction thresholds. |\n| `collect-redaction-calibration-inputs.ts` | Collects data used by redaction calibration runs. |\n| `run-phase2-closure-metrics.mjs` | Generates closure metrics for a named spec folder and writes them under that folder's `scratch/`. Takes the spec-folder path as its one argument. |\n| `import-policy-rules.ts` | Shared rule definitions used by the import policy checks. |\n| `import-policy-allowlist.json` | Stores temporary approved exceptions with owner and expiry metadata. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. COMMANDS\n\nRun from `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli` unless a command uses a repository-root path.\n\n```bash\nnpx tsx evals/check-no-mcp-lib-imports-ast.ts\n```\n\nExpected result: exits zero when eval scripts avoid restricted runtime imports or use valid allowlist entries.\n\n```bash\nnpx tsx evals/check-allowlist-expiry.ts\n```\n\nExpected result: warns on near-expiry exceptions and fails on expired exceptions.\n\n```bash\nnpx tsx evals/check-source-dist-alignment.ts\n```\n\nExpected result: exits zero when every runtime-critical dist artifact still has a matching source file, and reports a violation for each orphan left by a deleted or renamed source.\n\n```bash\nnode evals/run-phase2-closure-metrics.mjs specs/<track>/<packet>\n```\n\nExpected result: writes closure metrics into that spec folder's `scratch/` directory. Without the spec-folder argument it exits with a usage error.\n\n---\n\n## 5. BOUNDARIES\n\n| Boundary | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Public API | Eval scripts should use the runtime package's public API (`@spec-kit/runtime/api`) rather than internal runtime modules. |\n| Exceptions | Internal runtime access requires an allowlist entry with owner, reason and expiry. |\n| Data | Calibration and metrics scripts may read fixtures and write into a named spec folder's `scratch/`, but should not rewrite tracked artifacts unless a command documents that behavior. |\n| Reporting | Output should state when prerequisites are missing or results are investigation-only. |\n\n---\n\n## 6. VALIDATION\n\nRun the README validator after editing this file:\n\n```bash\npython3 .opencode/skills/sk-doc/scripts/validate_document.py .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/evals/README.md\n```\n\nRun policy checks after changing eval scripts:\n\n```bash\ncd .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli\nnpx tsx evals/check-no-mcp-lib-imports-ast.ts\nnpx tsx evals/check-allowlist-expiry.ts\n```\n\nExpected result: both policy checks exit zero or report a documented exception that needs review.\n\n---\n\n## 7. RELATED\n\n- [`../README.md`](../README.md)\n- [`../core/README.md`](../core/README.md)\n- [`../../ARCHITECTURE.md`](../../ARCHITECTURE.md)\n- [`import-policy-allowlist.json`](./import-policy-allowlist.json)","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":147,"totalLines":147,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/evals/README.md","time":{"start":1788625214875,"end":1788625214903}},"id":"prt_0725edd99001zSqYtCu8ts9i2f","sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","messageID":"msg_0725e6df90015NzU5Sme7JsUYf"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788625214907,"sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_FvgxPyuDNPEiQaxwgrcHp72Y","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/validation/README.md","offset":1,"limit":130},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/validation/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Validation Scripts: Spec Packet Checks\"\n3: description: \"CLI validators for comment hygiene, continuity freshness and evidence-marker integrity.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"ephemeral pointer audit\"\n6:   - \"comment hygiene\"\n7:   - \"continuity freshness\"\n8:   - \"evidence marker lint\"\n9:   - \"validation scripts\"\n10: ---\n11: \n12: # Validation Scripts: Spec Packet Checks\n13: \n14: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n15: \n16: `scripts/validation/` contains focused validators used by the Spec Kit validation flow, the pre-commit gate and the write-time comment-hygiene hook. The scripts produce structured pass / warn / fail output that shell wrappers and strict validation gates consume.\n17: \n18: Current responsibilities:\n19: \n20: - Flag code comments that embed ephemeral tracking-artifact pointers (spec numbers, task / checklist / requirement / ADR / review-finding ids).\n21: - Check whether continuity timestamps lag graph-metadata timestamps.\n22: - Audit `[EVIDENCE: ...]` markers across spec-packet markdown.\n23: - Bridge the runtime's generated-metadata drift and integrity checks into the `validate.sh` protocol.\n24: - Surface recorded failures (governance FAILs, loop-flagged contradictions, drift notes) that were written down but never routed to a remediation.\n25: \n26: ---\n27: \n28: ## 2. DIRECTORY TREE\n29: \n30: ```text\n31: validation/\n32: +-- ephemeral-pointer-audit.mjs             # Comment-hygiene guard (sk-code §4 enforcement)\n33: +-- continuity-freshness.ts                 # Continuity timestamp freshness validator\n34: +-- evidence-marker-audit.ts                # Evidence-marker parser, report and optional rewrap tool\n35: +-- generated-metadata-drift.ts             # validate.sh bridge for the generated-metadata drift gate\n36: +-- generated-metadata-integrity.ts         # validate.sh bridge for the generated-metadata integrity check\n37: +-- unactioned-recorded-failure-audit.mjs   # Finds recorded failures with no nearby remediation link\n38: `-- README.md\n39: ```\n40: \n41: ---\n42: \n43: ## 3. KEY FILES\n44: \n45: | File | Responsibility |\n46: |---|---|\n47: | `ephemeral-pointer-audit.mjs` | Standalone, dependency-free Node ESM guard that scans code comments only and flags pointers to ephemeral artifacts. Durable WHY comments and external standards (SHA-256, UTF-16, CWE, RFC) are explicitly allowed; the perishable traceability id is what it forbids. |\n48: | `continuity-freshness.ts` | Compares `_memory.continuity.last_updated_at` against the `graph-metadata.json` save time and reports lag. |\n49: | `evidence-marker-audit.ts` | Parses evidence markers while ignoring fenced and inline code; read-only unless `--rewrap` is supplied. |\n50: | `generated-metadata-drift.ts` | Re-derives a spec folder and compares stored `description.json` / `causal_summary` against a fresh derivation, ignoring volatile timestamps; report-only until the drift gate graduates to a hard failure. |\n51: | `generated-metadata-integrity.ts` | Validates `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json` against the shared schemas plus path-prefix and status-enum invariants; report-only until the migration graduates the rule to a hard error. |\n52: | `unactioned-recorded-failure-audit.mjs` | Scans markdown for recorded-failure language (FAIL, contradiction, drift, unactioned) with no nearby remediation link, biased toward over-flagging. |\n53: \n54: ---\n55: \n56: ## 4. COMMENT-HYGIENE GUARD\n57: \n58: `ephemeral-pointer-audit.mjs` is the runtime arm of the sk-code §4 \"No Ephemeral-Artifact Pointers\" rule (`.opencode/skills/sk-code/shared/references/universal/code-style-guide.md §4`). It is wired into the pre-commit gate and the write-time comment-hygiene hook.\n59: \n60: What it flags (inside comment regions only): a tracking word plus a number (\"spec 031\", \"phase 005\", \"packet 117\"), zero-padded spec/sub-phase pairs (\"029/003\"), spec slugs (\"031-embedding-stack-hardening\"), task ids (\"T043\"), checklist ids (\"CHK-160\"), requirement ids (\"REQ-005\"), ADR ids (\"ADR-004\"), review-finding ids (\"DR-008\", \"P0-3\", \"F-001-005\") and GitHub issue refs (\"#456\").\n61: \n62: What it deliberately does NOT flag: string/code content (only comments are inspected), durable structural numbers (HTTP codes, embedding dims, schema-version tags), `@example` / format-shape illustrations, runtime path constants the code reads, source line ranges, and externally versioned standards.\n63: \n64: Behavior worth knowing:\n65: \n66: - File selection is by extension (`.ts .tsx .js .jsx .mjs .cjs .py`) plus shebang detection for extensionless Node / Python scripts; `node_modules`, `.git`, `dist`, `build`, `coverage` and Python cache dirs are skipped.\n67: - The guard never flags itself (`ephemeral-pointer-audit.mjs` is excluded by name).\n68: - Exit codes: `0` clean, `1` violations found, `2` bad invocation (no paths). A non-code-only commit can still print a scary banner from upstream wrappers while this checker reports clean.\n69: \n70: ---\n71: \n72: ## 5. USAGE NOTES\n73: \n74: - Run these scripts against spec folders or source trees as noted; the audit recurses directories.\n75: - `evidence-marker-audit.ts` is read-only unless `--rewrap` is supplied.\n76: - `continuity-freshness.ts` treats missing optional files as skipped checks rather than hard failures.\n77: \n78: ---\n79: \n80: ## 6. VALIDATION\n81: \n82: Run from the repository root.\n83: \n84: Comment-hygiene smoke check over the spec-kit script tree:\n85: \n86: ```bash\n87: node .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/validation/ephemeral-pointer-audit.mjs \\\n88:   .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli\n89: echo $?   # 0 = clean, 1 = violations, 2 = bad invocation\n90: ```\n91: \n92: README structure check:\n93: \n94: ```bash\n95: python3 .opencode/skills/sk-doc/shared/scripts/validate_document.py \\\n96:   .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/validation/README.md\n97: ```\n98: \n99: Expected result: the audit exits `0` over a clean tree and the README validation exits `0`.\n100: \n101: ---\n102: \n103: ## 7. RELATED\n104: \n105: - [`scripts/`](../README.md)\n106: - [`ephemeral-pointer-audit.mjs`](./ephemeral-pointer-audit.mjs)\n107: - [`continuity-freshness.ts`](./continuity-freshness.ts)\n108: - [`evidence-marker-audit.ts`](./evidence-marker-audit.ts)\n109: - [`generated-metadata-drift.ts`](./generated-metadata-drift.ts)\n110: - [`generated-metadata-integrity.ts`](./generated-metadata-integrity.ts)\n111: - [`unactioned-recorded-failure-audit.mjs`](./unactioned-recorded-failure-audit.mjs)\n\n(End of file - total 111 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Validation Scripts: Spec Packet Checks\"\ndescription: \"CLI validators for comment hygiene, continuity freshness and evidence-marker integrity.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"ephemeral pointer audit\"\n  - \"comment hygiene\"\n  - \"continuity freshness\"\n  - \"evidence marker lint\"\n  - \"validation scripts\"\n---\n\n# Validation Scripts: Spec Packet Checks\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/validation/` contains focused validators used by the Spec Kit validation flow, the pre-commit gate and the write-time comment-hygiene hook. The scripts produce structured pass / warn / fail output that shell wrappers and strict validation gates consume.\n\nCurrent responsibilities:\n\n- Flag code comments that embed ephemeral tracking-artifact pointers (spec numbers, task / checklist / requirement / ADR / review-finding ids).","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/validation/README.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Validation Scripts: Spec Packet Checks\"\ndescription: \"CLI validators for comment hygiene, continuity freshness and evidence-marker integrity.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"ephemeral pointer audit\"\n  - \"comment hygiene\"\n  - \"continuity freshness\"\n  - \"evidence marker lint\"\n  - \"validation scripts\"\n---\n\n# Validation Scripts: Spec Packet Checks\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`scripts/validation/` contains focused validators used by the Spec Kit validation flow, the pre-commit gate and the write-time comment-hygiene hook. The scripts produce structured pass / warn / fail output that shell wrappers and strict validation gates consume.\n\nCurrent responsibilities:\n\n- Flag code comments that embed ephemeral tracking-artifact pointers (spec numbers, task / checklist / requirement / ADR / review-finding ids).\n- Check whether continuity timestamps lag graph-metadata timestamps.\n- Audit `[EVIDENCE: ...]` markers across spec-packet markdown.\n- Bridge the runtime's generated-metadata drift and integrity checks into the `validate.sh` protocol.\n- Surface recorded failures (governance FAILs, loop-flagged contradictions, drift notes) that were written down but never routed to a remediation.\n\n---\n\n## 2. DIRECTORY TREE\n\n```text\nvalidation/\n+-- ephemeral-pointer-audit.mjs             # Comment-hygiene guard (sk-code §4 enforcement)\n+-- continuity-freshness.ts                 # Continuity timestamp freshness validator\n+-- evidence-marker-audit.ts                # Evidence-marker parser, report and optional rewrap tool\n+-- generated-metadata-drift.ts             # validate.sh bridge for the generated-metadata drift gate\n+-- generated-metadata-integrity.ts         # validate.sh bridge for the generated-metadata integrity check\n+-- unactioned-recorded-failure-audit.mjs   # Finds recorded failures with no nearby remediation link\n`-- README.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `ephemeral-pointer-audit.mjs` | Standalone, dependency-free Node ESM guard that scans code comments only and flags pointers to ephemeral artifacts. Durable WHY comments and external standards (SHA-256, UTF-16, CWE, RFC) are explicitly allowed; the perishable traceability id is what it forbids. |\n| `continuity-freshness.ts` | Compares `_memory.continuity.last_updated_at` against the `graph-metadata.json` save time and reports lag. |\n| `evidence-marker-audit.ts` | Parses evidence markers while ignoring fenced and inline code; read-only unless `--rewrap` is supplied. |\n| `generated-metadata-drift.ts` | Re-derives a spec folder and compares stored `description.json` / `causal_summary` against a fresh derivation, ignoring volatile timestamps; report-only until the drift gate graduates to a hard failure. |\n| `generated-metadata-integrity.ts` | Validates `description.json` and `graph-metadata.json` against the shared schemas plus path-prefix and status-enum invariants; report-only until the migration graduates the rule to a hard error. |\n| `unactioned-recorded-failure-audit.mjs` | Scans markdown for recorded-failure language (FAIL, contradiction, drift, unactioned) with no nearby remediation link, biased toward over-flagging. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. COMMENT-HYGIENE GUARD\n\n`ephemeral-pointer-audit.mjs` is the runtime arm of the sk-code §4 \"No Ephemeral-Artifact Pointers\" rule (`.opencode/skills/sk-code/shared/references/universal/code-style-guide.md §4`). It is wired into the pre-commit gate and the write-time comment-hygiene hook.\n\nWhat it flags (inside comment regions only): a tracking word plus a number (\"spec 031\", \"phase 005\", \"packet 117\"), zero-padded spec/sub-phase pairs (\"029/003\"), spec slugs (\"031-embedding-stack-hardening\"), task ids (\"T043\"), checklist ids (\"CHK-160\"), requirement ids (\"REQ-005\"), ADR ids (\"ADR-004\"), review-finding ids (\"DR-008\", \"P0-3\", \"F-001-005\") and GitHub issue refs (\"#456\").\n\nWhat it deliberately does NOT flag: string/code content (only comments are inspected), durable structural numbers (HTTP codes, embedding dims, schema-version tags), `@example` / format-shape illustrations, runtime path constants the code reads, source line ranges, and externally versioned standards.\n\nBehavior worth knowing:\n\n- File selection is by extension (`.ts .tsx .js .jsx .mjs .cjs .py`) plus shebang detection for extensionless Node / Python scripts; `node_modules`, `.git`, `dist`, `build`, `coverage` and Python cache dirs are skipped.\n- The guard never flags itself (`ephemeral-pointer-audit.mjs` is excluded by name).\n- Exit codes: `0` clean, `1` violations found, `2` bad invocation (no paths). A non-code-only commit can still print a scary banner from upstream wrappers while this checker reports clean.\n\n---\n\n## 5. USAGE NOTES\n\n- Run these scripts against spec folders or source trees as noted; the audit recurses directories.\n- `evidence-marker-audit.ts` is read-only unless `--rewrap` is supplied.\n- `continuity-freshness.ts` treats missing optional files as skipped checks rather than hard failures.\n\n---\n\n## 6. VALIDATION\n\nRun from the repository root.\n\nComment-hygiene smoke check over the spec-kit script tree:\n\n```bash\nnode .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/validation/ephemeral-pointer-audit.mjs \\\n  .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli\necho $?   # 0 = clean, 1 = violations, 2 = bad invocation\n```\n\nREADME structure check:\n\n```bash\npython3 .opencode/skills/sk-doc/shared/scripts/validate_document.py \\\n  .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/validation/README.md\n```\n\nExpected result: the audit exits `0` over a clean tree and the README validation exits `0`.\n\n---\n\n## 7. RELATED\n\n- [`scripts/`](../README.md)\n- [`ephemeral-pointer-audit.mjs`](./ephemeral-pointer-audit.mjs)\n- [`continuity-freshness.ts`](./continuity-freshness.ts)\n- [`evidence-marker-audit.ts`](./evidence-marker-audit.ts)\n- [`generated-metadata-drift.ts`](./generated-metadata-drift.ts)\n- [`generated-metadata-integrity.ts`](./generated-metadata-integrity.ts)\n- [`unactioned-recorded-failure-audit.mjs`](./unactioned-recorded-failure-audit.mjs)","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":111,"totalLines":111,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/validation/README.md","time":{"start":1788625214868,"end":1788625214904}},"id":"prt_0725edd920013MVPH0WB8W0ZDT","sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","messageID":"msg_0725e6df90015NzU5Sme7JsUYf"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788625214907,"sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_VWpcH3JZ3ic9RjSFVt9QauW2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-validation.js","offset":1,"limit":100},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-validation.js</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: #!/usr/bin/env node\n2: // ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n3: // ║ COMPONENT: Phase Validation Tests                                        ║\n4: // ╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣\n5: // ║ PURPOSE: Validate phase-level rules and recursive validation behavior.   ║\n6: // ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n7: 'use strict';\n8: \n9: const fs = require('fs');\n10: const os = require('os');\n11: const path = require('path');\n12: const { execFileSync } = require('child_process');\n13: \n14: const REPO_ROOT = path.resolve(__dirname, '..', '..', '..', '..', '..', '..');\n15: const SKILL_ROOT = path.join(REPO_ROOT, '.opencode', 'skills', 'system-spec-kit');\n16: const CREATE_SCRIPT = path.join(SKILL_ROOT, 'runtime', 'cli', 'spec', 'create.sh');\n17: const RECOMMEND_SCRIPT = path.join(SKILL_ROOT, 'runtime', 'cli', 'spec', 'recommend-level.sh');\n18: const VALIDATE_SCRIPT = path.join(SKILL_ROOT, 'runtime', 'cli', 'spec', 'validate.sh');\n19: const ARCHIVE_SCRIPT = path.join(SKILL_ROOT, 'runtime', 'cli', 'spec', 'archive.sh');\n20: const FIXTURE_ROOT = path.join(SKILL_ROOT, 'runtime', 'cli', 'tests', 'fixtures');\n21: const ALLOWED_SPECS_ROOT = path.join(REPO_ROOT, '.opencode', 'specs');\n22: \n23: let passed = 0;\n24: let failed = 0;\n25: \n26: function pass(message) {\n27:   passed += 1;\n28:   console.log(`PASS: ${message}`);\n29: }\n30: \n31: function fail(message) {\n32:   failed += 1;\n33:   console.log(`FAIL: ${message}`);\n34: }\n35: \n36: function assertEqual(actual, expected, message) {\n37:   if (actual === expected) {\n38:     pass(message);\n39:   } else {\n40:     fail(`${message} (expected=${expected}, actual=${actual})`);\n41:   }\n42: }\n43: \n44: function assertTrue(condition, message) {\n45:   if (condition) {\n46:     pass(message);\n47:   } else {\n48:     fail(message);\n49:   }\n50: }\n51: \n52: function runBash(scriptPath, args, cwd = REPO_ROOT) {\n53:   return execFileSync('bash', [scriptPath, ...args], {\n54:     cwd,\n55:     encoding: 'utf-8',\n56:   });\n57: }\n58: \n59: function runBashExpectFailure(scriptPath, args, cwd = REPO_ROOT) {\n60:   try {\n61:     runBash(scriptPath, args, cwd);\n62:     return { code: 0, stdout: '', stderr: '' };\n63:   } catch (error) {\n64:     return {\n65:       code: error.status || 1,\n66:       stdout: error.stdout || '',\n67:       stderr: error.stderr || '',\n68:     };\n69:   }\n70: }\n71: \n72: function parseJson(raw, message) {\n73:   const trimmed = raw.trim();\n74: \n75:   try {\n76:     return JSON.parse(trimmed);\n77:   } catch {\n78:     // Some scripts may emit status lines before JSON payloads.\n79:     const start = trimmed.indexOf('{');\n80:     const end = trimmed.lastIndexOf('}');\n81: \n82:     if (start !== -1 && end !== -1 && end > start) {\n83:       const candidate = trimmed.slice(start, end + 1);\n84:       try {\n85:         return JSON.parse(candidate);\n86:       } catch {\n87:         // Fall through to detailed error.\n88:       }\n89:     }\n90:   }\n91: \n92:   try {\n93:     return JSON.parse(raw);\n94:   } catch (error) {\n95:     const reason = error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error);\n96:     throw new Error(`${message}: ${reason}\\nRaw output:\\n${raw}`);\n97:   }\n98: }\n99: \n100: function loadFixture(relativePath) {\n\n(Showing lines 1-100 of 440. Use offset=101 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n// ║ COMPONENT: Phase Validation Tests                                        ║\n// ╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣\n// ║ PURPOSE: Validate phase-level rules and recursive validation behavior.   ║\n// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n'use strict';\n\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst os = require('os');\nconst path = require('path');\nconst { execFileSync } = require('child_process');\n\nconst REPO_ROOT = path.resolve(__dirname, '..', '..', '..', '..', '..', '..');\nconst SKILL_ROOT = path.join(REPO_ROOT, '.opencode', 'skills', 'system-spec-kit');\nconst CREATE_SCRIPT = path.join(SKILL_ROOT, 'runtime', 'cli', 'spec', 'create.sh');\nconst RECOMMEND_SCRIPT = path.join(SKILL_ROOT, 'runtime', 'cli', 'spec', 'recommend-level.sh');\nconst VALIDATE_SCRIPT = path.join(SKILL_ROOT, 'runtime', 'cli', 'spec', 'validate.sh');\nconst ARCHIVE_SCRIPT = path.join(SKILL_ROOT, 'runtime', 'cli', 'spec', 'archive.sh');\nconst FIXTURE_ROOT = path.join(SKILL_ROOT, 'runtime', 'cli', 'tests', 'fixtures');","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-validation.js","text":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n// ║ COMPONENT: Phase Validation Tests                                        ║\n// ╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣\n// ║ PURPOSE: Validate phase-level rules and recursive validation behavior.   ║\n// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n'use strict';\n\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst os = require('os');\nconst path = require('path');\nconst { execFileSync } = require('child_process');\n\nconst REPO_ROOT = path.resolve(__dirname, '..', '..', '..', '..', '..', '..');\nconst SKILL_ROOT = path.join(REPO_ROOT, '.opencode', 'skills', 'system-spec-kit');\nconst CREATE_SCRIPT = path.join(SKILL_ROOT, 'runtime', 'cli', 'spec', 'create.sh');\nconst RECOMMEND_SCRIPT = path.join(SKILL_ROOT, 'runtime', 'cli', 'spec', 'recommend-level.sh');\nconst VALIDATE_SCRIPT = path.join(SKILL_ROOT, 'runtime', 'cli', 'spec', 'validate.sh');\nconst ARCHIVE_SCRIPT = path.join(SKILL_ROOT, 'runtime', 'cli', 'spec', 'archive.sh');\nconst FIXTURE_ROOT = path.join(SKILL_ROOT, 'runtime', 'cli', 'tests', 'fixtures');\nconst ALLOWED_SPECS_ROOT = path.join(REPO_ROOT, '.opencode', 'specs');\n\nlet passed = 0;\nlet failed = 0;\n\nfunction pass(message) {\n  passed += 1;\n  console.log(`PASS: ${message}`);\n}\n\nfunction fail(message) {\n  failed += 1;\n  console.log(`FAIL: ${message}`);\n}\n\nfunction assertEqual(actual, expected, message) {\n  if (actual === expected) {\n    pass(message);\n  } else {\n    fail(`${message} (expected=${expected}, actual=${actual})`);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction assertTrue(condition, message) {\n  if (condition) {\n    pass(message);\n  } else {\n    fail(message);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction runBash(scriptPath, args, cwd = REPO_ROOT) {\n  return execFileSync('bash', [scriptPath, ...args], {\n    cwd,\n    encoding: 'utf-8',\n  });\n}\n\nfunction runBashExpectFailure(scriptPath, args, cwd = REPO_ROOT) {\n  try {\n    runBash(scriptPath, args, cwd);\n    return { code: 0, stdout: '', stderr: '' };\n  } catch (error) {\n    return {\n      code: error.status || 1,\n      stdout: error.stdout || '',\n      stderr: error.stderr || '',\n    };\n  }\n}\n\nfunction parseJson(raw, message) {\n  const trimmed = raw.trim();\n\n  try {\n    return JSON.parse(trimmed);\n  } catch {\n    // Some scripts may emit status lines before JSON payloads.\n    const start = trimmed.indexOf('{');\n    const end = trimmed.lastIndexOf('}');\n\n    if (start !== -1 && end !== -1 && end > start) {\n      const candidate = trimmed.slice(start, end + 1);\n      try {\n        return JSON.parse(candidate);\n      } catch {\n        // Fall through to detailed error.\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  try {\n    return JSON.parse(raw);\n  } catch (error) {\n    const reason = error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error);\n    throw new Error(`${message}: ${reason}\\nRaw output:\\n${raw}`);\n  }\n}\n\nfunction loadFixture(relativePath) {","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":100,"totalLines":440,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-phase-validation.js","time":{"start":1788625214883,"end":1788625214905}},"id":"prt_0725edda2001fege5e59RubKjw","sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","messageID":"msg_0725e6df90015NzU5Sme7JsUYf"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788625214910,"sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_GgWdy6y1pHRqRx1L2GMKdcMX","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-scripts-modules.js","offset":1,"limit":80},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-scripts-modules.js</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: // 1. TEST: SCRIPTS MODULES COMPREHENSIVE VERIFICATION\n3: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: 'use strict';\n5: \n6: import { createRequire } from 'node:module';\n7: import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n8: \n9: const require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\n10: const __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);\n11: const path = require('path');\n12: const fs = require('fs');\n13: const __dirname = path.dirname(__filename);\n14: \n15: /* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n16:    1. CONFIGURATION\n17: ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n18: */\n19: \n20: const SCRIPTS_DIR = path.join(__dirname, '..', 'dist');\n21: const ROOT = path.join(__dirname, '..', '..');\n22: \n23: // Test results tracking\n24: const results = {\n25:   passed: 0,\n26:   failed: 0,\n27:   skipped: 0,\n28:   tests: [],\n29: };\n30: \n31: /* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n32:    2. TEST UTILITIES\n33: ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n34: */\n35: \n36: function log(msg) {\n37:   console.log(msg);\n38: }\n39: \n40: function pass(testName, evidence) {\n41:   results.passed++;\n42:   results.tests.push({ name: testName, status: 'PASS', evidence });\n43:   log(`   ✅ ${testName}`);\n44:   if (evidence) log(`      Evidence: ${evidence}`);\n45: }\n46: \n47: function fail(testName, reason) {\n48:   results.failed++;\n49:   results.tests.push({ name: testName, status: 'FAIL', reason });\n50:   log(`   ❌ ${testName}`);\n51:   log(`      Reason: ${reason}`);\n52: }\n53: \n54: function skip(testName, reason) {\n55:   results.skipped++;\n56:   results.tests.push({ name: testName, status: 'SKIP', reason });\n57:   log(`   ⏭️  ${testName} (skipped: ${reason})`);\n58: }\n59: \n60: function assertExists(value, testName, evidence) {\n61:   if (value !== undefined && value !== null) {\n62:     pass(testName, evidence);\n63:     return true;\n64:   } else {\n65:     fail(testName, 'Value is undefined or null');\n66:     return false;\n67:   }\n68: }\n69: \n70: function assertEqual(actual, expected, testName) {\n71:   if (actual === expected) {\n72:     pass(testName, `${actual} === ${expected}`);\n73:     return true;\n74:   } else {\n75:     fail(testName, `Expected ${expected}, got ${actual}`);\n76:     return false;\n77:   }\n78: }\n79: \n80: function assertType(value, expectedType, testName) {\n\n(Showing lines 1-80 of 3135. Use offset=81 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. TEST: SCRIPTS MODULES COMPREHENSIVE VERIFICATION\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n'use strict';\n\nimport { createRequire } from 'node:module';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n\nconst require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\nconst __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);\nconst path = require('path');\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst __dirname = path.dirname(__filename);\n\n/* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n   1. CONFIGURATION\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n*/\n\nconst SCRIPTS_DIR = path.join(__dirname, '..', 'dist');","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-scripts-modules.js","text":"// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. TEST: SCRIPTS MODULES COMPREHENSIVE VERIFICATION\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n'use strict';\n\nimport { createRequire } from 'node:module';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n\nconst require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\nconst __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);\nconst path = require('path');\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst __dirname = path.dirname(__filename);\n\n/* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n   1. CONFIGURATION\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n*/\n\nconst SCRIPTS_DIR = path.join(__dirname, '..', 'dist');\nconst ROOT = path.join(__dirname, '..', '..');\n\n// Test results tracking\nconst results = {\n  passed: 0,\n  failed: 0,\n  skipped: 0,\n  tests: [],\n};\n\n/* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n   2. TEST UTILITIES\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n*/\n\nfunction log(msg) {\n  console.log(msg);\n}\n\nfunction pass(testName, evidence) {\n  results.passed++;\n  results.tests.push({ name: testName, status: 'PASS', evidence });\n  log(`   ✅ ${testName}`);\n  if (evidence) log(`      Evidence: ${evidence}`);\n}\n\nfunction fail(testName, reason) {\n  results.failed++;\n  results.tests.push({ name: testName, status: 'FAIL', reason });\n  log(`   ❌ ${testName}`);\n  log(`      Reason: ${reason}`);\n}\n\nfunction skip(testName, reason) {\n  results.skipped++;\n  results.tests.push({ name: testName, status: 'SKIP', reason });\n  log(`   ⏭️  ${testName} (skipped: ${reason})`);\n}\n\nfunction assertExists(value, testName, evidence) {\n  if (value !== undefined && value !== null) {\n    pass(testName, evidence);\n    return true;\n  } else {\n    fail(testName, 'Value is undefined or null');\n    return false;\n  }\n}\n\nfunction assertEqual(actual, expected, testName) {\n  if (actual === expected) {\n    pass(testName, `${actual} === ${expected}`);\n    return true;\n  } else {\n    fail(testName, `Expected ${expected}, got ${actual}`);\n    return false;\n  }\n}\n\nfunction assertType(value, expectedType, testName) {","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":80,"totalLines":3135,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/test-scripts-modules.js","time":{"start":1788625214885,"end":1788625214909}},"id":"prt_0725edda4001Wl7RiXgrxrfzMN","sessionID":"ses_f8da76375ffeCjuPpA01WdxIjC","messageID":"msg_0725e6df90015NzU5Sme7JsUYf"}}
